 \"text\": \"Resolution-date note: the canonical ledger target uses 2026-12-15, tied to CMS's monthly data.Medicaid.gov release vehicle for a three-to-four-month-lag August 2026 first print. I did not find a separate future-dated CMS placeholder in this sandbox; I keep the target's date and bind scoring to the first official CMS dataset print.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/codex_last_message.txt:1:{\"schemaVersion\":\"brier_reasoning_judge_v1\",\"summary\":\"Across the 8 reviewed CMS Medicaid ex parte renewal-share traces, Brier generally identified the correct state-row resolver, used official CMS/data.medicaid.gov context, anchored forecasts in state-specific recent history, and incorporated pre-submit reviewer feedback into more auditable prior/update/interval explanations. The main system weaknesses are repeated: catalog lookups sometimes expose prior point/interval values that exactly match the final forecast and create circularity risk; the strict first-print original-submission resolver repeatedly drifted into same-release-day correction exceptions before review; sparse historical samples were used without a structured representation of missing months, vintage status, and volatility method; and high-ceiling percentage targets need a more standardized bounded-interval calibration. These are fixable with prompt changes, validators, and CMS-specific source adapter fields rather than case-by-case reviewer intervention.\",\"reviewedRunCount\":8,\"strengths\":[\"Most traces correctly treated the target as a single state row rather than a national average.\",\"The runs consistently used CMS/data.medicaid.gov as the resolution source rather than relying on secondary mirrors.\",\"Reasoning usually named recent state-specific observations and used latest-value persistence or damped local trend as the baseline.\",\"Pre-submit review caught several concrete issues, and final traces often recorded accepted fixes in the review disposition.\",\"Several runs explicitly noted that 2026-12-15 is ledger-based because no future CMS placeholder was found, improving auditability of the schedule assumption.\",\"High-share states generally recognized the 100 percent mechanical ceiling and made intervals asymmetric or capped.\"],\"systemIssues\":[{\"issueId\":\"catalog_prior_circularity\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Several traces fetched registered catalog point estimates and intervals that exactly matched the final forecast, making the reasoning appear circular even when later text claimed independent derivation.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"issueId\":\"first_print_rule_drift\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"area\":\"validator\",\"summary\":\"The first-print original-submission resolver repeatedly acquired same-release-day correction exceptions or ambiguous correction language that conflicted with the canonical ledger rule.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"issueId\":\"sparse_history_unstructured\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"data_adapter\",\"summary\":\"Runs relied on sparse five-point historical samples but did not have a structured way to declare whether skipped months were unavailable, intentionally excluded, preliminary, original, or latest inspected.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"issueId\":\"interval_calibration_is_judgmental\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Interval widths were often justified after the fact from sparse moves, missing-month uncertainty, and cohort risk without a consistent named calibration rule or volatility statistic.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"issueId\":\"bounded_percent_targets_need_policy\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"pack\",\"summary\":\"High-share percentage targets near 100 percent used ad hoc ceiling caps, commonly 99.0, without a standardized bounded-distribution or tail-mass convention.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"issueId\":\"wrong_vintage_source_context\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"data_adapter\",\"summary\":\"Some source contexts included preliminary-status CMS URLs while the resolver required original O rows, forcing the reasoning to clarify that those links were only for release timing.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\"]},{\"issueId\":\"reviewer_findings_repeat\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"validator\",\"summary\":\"The same reviewer findings recurred across runs, especially resolver correction exceptions, catalog circularity, and sparse interval explanations, indicating they should be enforced before pre-submit review.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]}],\"recommendations\":[{\"priority\":\"now\",\"area\":\"validator\",\"summary\":\"Block same-day correction exceptions for strict first-print targets.\",\"rationale\":\"The resolution value must be mechanically reproducible. Allowing corrections within a release day creates cutoff and timezone ambiguity and repeatedly required reviewer correction.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Add a validator rule for targets with resolutionRule containing first print, first publication, or original (O): reject reasoning or normalized cells whose resolutionRule includes phrases such as same release day, same-day correction, corrected before release day ends, or unless CMS corrects, unless the target ledger explicitly contains that exception.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Cleaner resolver text and fewer repeated pre-submit warnings on CMS first-print targets.\",\"risk\":\"Some official datasets may publish corrected files under the same timestamp; those cases would need an explicit ledger flag rather than free-text exceptions.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"now\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Forbid using catalog point estimates and intervals as forecast evidence.\",\"rationale\":\"The forecast trace should be independently auditable. Showing prior catalog values that match the final output makes it unclear whether Brier reasoned or copied.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Amend the analyst prompt: catalog or ledger lookup may verify slug, unit, dataPointId, resolver, source, and resolution date only. If pointEstimate, ciLow, or ciHigh are present in local catalog context, ignore them and do not include them in tool results or reasoning unless explicitly auditing an existing catalog forecast.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Removes circular-looking traces and improves trust in generated forecasts.\",\"risk\":\"The model loses access to useful baselines from previous forecasts; if needed, expose them through a separate labeled comparison track, not the main forecast evidence track.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"now\",\"area\":\"data_adapter\",\"summary\":\"Add a CMS Medicaid PI history adapter that returns structured vintage-aware observations.\",\"rationale\":\"The fast public-release prompt is a reasonable match for CMS series, but the repeated sparse-history caveats show the agent lacks a clean history table with month coverage and submission status.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Implement an adapter output object with fields: state, reportingPeriod, value, numerator, denominator, submissionStatus, firstPrintObservedAt, sourceUrl, isMissingMonth, missingReason, and vintageType. Provide the last N monthly original/O observations plus explicit unavailable months to the analyst prompt.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Better trend and volatility estimates, fewer ambiguous statements about inspected samples, and easier audit of first-print versus preliminary values.\",\"risk\":\"Requires adapter maintenance when CMS schema or datastore identifiers change.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"next\",\"area\":\"pack\",\"summary\":\"Create a bounded-percentage interval pack for shares near 0 or 100 percent.\",\"rationale\":\"Several high-share states used judgmental 99.0 caps. A standard method would improve calibration consistency and make tail treatment auditable.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Add a pack that instructs Brier to model percentage shares on a logit or clipped-beta scale when point estimates are above 85 percent or below 15 percent, then transform back to percent and report whether bounds are distribution-derived or policy-capped.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"More coherent asymmetric intervals for Arizona, California, Connecticut, DC, and similar ceiling-constrained series.\",\"risk\":\"May over-formalize sparse administrative series if the transformed model is presented with false precision; prompt should require a plain-language caveat.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"next\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Require a structured prior-update-interval block with named components.\",\"rationale\":\"The reviewed traces improved after reviewer intervention, but many initial weaknesses were about unclear update sizes and interval mapping. Making the representation mandatory should reduce repeated warnings.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Require fields in reasoning: historyWindow, observationsUsed, missingObservationPolicy, priorAnchor, updateComponents with signed pp values, volatilityStatistic, intervalExpansionFactors, boundedTargetAdjustment, and finalArithmetic.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"More comparable traces across states and easier automated review of arbitrary judgmental adjustments.\",\"risk\":\"Longer traces and possible boilerplate if the fast prompt overuses the structure on simple stable series.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"next\",\"area\":\"validator\",\"summary\":\"Detect repeated reviewer findings and promote them to automatic checks.\",\"rationale\":\"Pre-submit review repeatedly caught the same classes of issues. These should be deterministic checks where possible, freeing review for substantive reasoning quality.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Add reviewer-finding aggregation by rubricItem and phrase signature. When a warning appears in three or more recent runs for the same series family, open a validator suggestion or fail condition, starting with resolver exceptions, catalog prior references, and missing sample-size statements.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Reduces manual review churn and prevents known problems from recurring in batch runs.\",\"risk\":\"Phrase-based detection can be brittle; use structured fields where available and keep the initial mode as warning-only before blocking.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"later\",\"area\":\"ui\",\"summary\":\"Show source vintage and missing-history coverage on forecast detail pages.\",\"rationale\":\"Readers need to distinguish official source evidence, local derived history, preliminary release timing links, and original-resolution rows.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Add a compact evidence table on run detail pages with columns for source type, reporting period, submission status, value role, and whether it was used for target resolution, history, timing, or only target registration.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Improves auditability and makes circularity or wrong-vintage evidence easier to spot visually.\",\"risk\":\"Adds UI density; keep it collapsed or grouped for long traces.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\"]}],\"promptPatchCandidates\":[{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"Add: For ledger/catalog lookups, use only target identity fields such as slug, unit, dataPointId, resolution source, resolution rule, and resolution date. Do not read, quote, or use existing catalog point estimates or intervals as evidence for a new forecast unless the task is explicitly to review an existing forecast.\"},{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"Add: For first-print or original-vintage targets, copy the ledger resolver exactly in substance. Do not add same-day correction, later correction, or release-day grace exceptions unless the registered target rule explicitly includes them.\"},{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"Add a required prior/update/interval section with: observations used, observations unavailable or skipped, prior anchor, signed update components, volatility statistic, interval expansion rationale, bounded-target adjustment, and final arithmetic.\"},{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"Add: When a source URL uses a different vintage, status, or filter from the resolver, label its role explicitly, for example release timing only, not historical value source or resolver evidence.\"},{\"file\":\"CMS Medicaid PI prompt pack or source adapter prompt\",\"patchSummary\":\"Expose a structured CMS history table for the requested state and measure, including reporting period, original/preliminary/updated status, numerator, denominator, computed share, first observed date, and missing-month reason. Instruct the analyst to prefer this table over ad hoc sparse catalog context.\"}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-31-57z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ga-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/revision_prompt.md:20:- resolutionDate: \"2026-12-15\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-31-57z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ga-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/revision_prompt.md:105:- resolutionDate must be verified from an official release calendar or announcement schedule this run. Do not infer it from cadence.\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-31-57z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ga-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/revision_prompt.md:126:{\"slug\":\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ga\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"Georgia Medicaid ex parte renewal share, Aug. 2026\",\"question\":\"CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data, Georgia state row, August 2026 reporting period, original first-print submission: ex parte renewals as a share of completed Medicaid renewals.\",\"unit\":\"percent\",\"pointEstimate\":83.6,\"ciLow\":78.2,\"ciHigh\":88.9,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-12-15\",\"resolutionSource\":\"CMS, State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data (data.medicaid.gov)\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to Georgia's August 2026 reporting-period original (O) state row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c when CMS first publishes that row. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published ex parte renewal numerator divided by the published completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS print available on data.medicaid.gov and ignore later updated submissions or revisions.\",\"dataPointId\":\"cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ga.aug_2026\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"GA 2025-07 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":77.3},{\"label\":\"GA 2025-09 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":78.2},{\"label\":\"GA 2025-11 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":81.1},{\"label\":\"GA 2026-01 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":82.2},{\"label\":\"GA 2026-02 latest inspected ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":81.6}],\"drivers\":[\"Georgia's recent ex parte renewal share is already high, around the low 80s\",\"Trend from July 2025 to early 2026 is positive but flattening\",\"Renewal cohort composition can move numerator and denominator month to month\",\"Data-match coverage and eligibility-system operations govern further gains\",\"Ceiling effects limit upside relative to lower-performing states\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-28T00:33:02Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for Georgia Medicaid ex parte renewal share, August 2026\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is a Georgia state row, not a national weighted average: the original first-publication August 2026 reporting-period row in the CMS eligibility processing dataset. The target is the share of completed Medicaid renewals processed ex parte, reported in percent and rounded to one decimal.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Inspected the registered CMS Medicaid PI target and local ledger identity fields for the Georgia August 2026 ex parte renewal-share resolver.\",\"result\":\"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ga, unit percent, registered resolutionDate 2026-12-15, dataset id 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ga.aug_2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked CMS Medicaid release vehicle context preserved for this data family.\",\"result\":\"Fetched official release context that data.Medicaid.gov is updated monthly; inspected CMS page context listed Preliminary March 2026 data and June 26, 2026 as the current update date for related February 2026 and March 2026 entries.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked CMS eligibility-processing resolver fields used for this ex parte renewal-share target.\",\"result\":\"Fetched original submission status O, August 2026 reporting period, numerator as completed renewals processed through ex parte renewal, denominator as total completed renewals, and expected publication lag of about 3 to 4 months after the reporting period.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"repo.lookup\",\"call\":\"Read the local official-source-derived Georgia historical context for this exact CMS series.\",\"result\":\"Fetched Georgia values: 2025-07 = 77.3 percent, 2025-09 = 78.2 percent, 2025-11 = 81.1 percent, 2026-01 = 82.2 percent, and 2026-02 = 81.6 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"repo.lookup\",\"call\":\"Computed recent Georgia movement and latest-value anchor from the inspected sample.\",\"result\":\"Fetched latest inspected Georgia value 2026-02 = 81.6 percent; changes were +0.9 percentage points from 2025-07 to 2025-09, +2.9 from 2025-09 to 2025-11, +1.1 from 2025-11 to 2026-01, and -0.6 from 2026-01 to 2026-02.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference class: the most relevant outside view is Georgia's own recent first-print run for this CMS eligibility-processing series. The five observed points average 80.1 percent, the latest three average 81.6 percent, and the latest inspected value is 81.6 percent, so latest-value persistence with modest trend continuation is the prior.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, and mechanism: Georgia is already a high ex parte performer, so ceiling effects matter. The July-to-January improvement supports a mild upward update, but the February dip and high starting level argue against extrapolating the full 2025 trend through August.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: prior model is Georgia latest-value persistence with damped local trend, using five inspected observations from 2025-07, 2025-09, 2025-11, 2026-01, and 2026-02. Starting from latest inspected 81.6 percent, I add +1.4 pp for the 2025-to-early-2026 improvement signal and +0.6 pp for CMS compliance and continued automation drift, yielding 83.6. The 80% interval is calibrated from realized first-print movements and widened for the six-month horizon, renewal-cohort mix, and limited skipped-month sample, giving 78.2 to 88.9.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: the forecast could be too high if the 2026-01 and 2026-02 values already represent Georgia's practical ceiling or if August has a manual-heavy renewal cohort. Upside outside the interval would require a durable system or data-match improvement pushing the first print above 88.9 percent; downside outside the interval would require a data-source outage, eligibility-system issue, reporting break, or cohort mix pushing the share below 78.2 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Historical mean = (77.3 + 78.2 + 81.1 + 82.2 + 81.6) / 5 = 80.1 percent. Adjacent changes were +0.9, +2.9, +1.1, and -0.6 pp, with mean absolute change about 1.4 pp. Point calculation: 81.6 latest inspected value + 1.4 pp damped trend + 0.6 pp automation/compliance drift = 83.6 percent. Interval calculation: center 83.6, lower half-width 5.4 pp and upper half-width 5.3 pp, yielding 78.2 to 88.9 after one-decimal rounding.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resolution-date note: the canonical ledger target uses 2026-12-15, tied to CMS's monthly data.Medicaid.gov release vehicle for a three-to-four-month-lag August 2026 first print. I did not find a separate future-dated CMS placeholder in this sandbox; I keep the target's date and bind scoring to the first official CMS dataset print.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":83.6,\"ciLow\":78.2,\"ciHigh\":88.9}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-16/2026-06-16t12-33-11z-us-dol-initial-claims-sa-week-2026-06-13/stderr.txt:98:- resolutionDate must be verified from an official release calendar or announcement schedule