value\":16.01,\"probability\":0.987692307692},{\"value\":16.04,\"probability\":0.989230769231},{\"value\":16.07,\"probability\":0.990769230769},{\"value\":16.1,\"probability\":0.992307692308},{\"value\":16.13,\"probability\":0.993846153846},{\"value\":16.16,\"probability\":0.995384615385},{\"value\":16.19,\"probability\":0.996923076923},{\"value\":16.22,\"probability\":0.998461538462},{\"value\":16.25,\"probability\":1}],\"summary\":{\"pointEstimate\":13,\"median\":13,\"interval80\":{\"lower\":11.9,\"upper\":14.3}},\"provenance\":\"interval_seeded\"},\"confidence\":0.8,\"publicTrace\":[\"Census release evidence was fetched from the income/poverty schedule and SPM tables pages; the target is the calendar-year 2025 SPM child poverty rate expected in September 2026.\",\"The recent Census history seed is 13.4% in 2024, with a 13.2% average over 2022-2024 after the expanded-CTC year.\",\"PolicyEngine current-law policy 2 (Current law) was verified live. The calibration fallback blends that current-law prior with recent SPM history and carries this run because AI Gateway call failed: Free tier users do not have access to this model. Upgrade to paid credits at https://vercel.com/d?to=%2F%5Bteam%5D%2F%7E%2Fai%3Fmodal%3Dtop-up for unrestricted access.\"],\"assumptions\":[\"Calendar-year 2025 policy is closer to the 2022-2024 current-law regime than to the 2021 expanded Child Tax Credit regime.\",\"Labor-market and real-earnings conditions keep the central estimate near, but slightly below, the latest published child SPM rate.\",\"ASEC sampling error and SPM expense adjustments justify an asymmetric interval around the point estimate.\"],\"dataCaveats\":[\"The Census pages are fetched live; the child-poverty history is a prototype seed until the API uses a machine-readable Census SPM table endpoint.\",\"The PolicyEngine input currently verifies current law and contributes a stored poverty prior; it is not yet a fresh server-side microsimulation run for this cell.\",\"SPM estimates include taxes, transfers, work expenses, medical out-of-pocket expenses, and geographic housing adjustments, so policy and price changes can move the series differently from official poverty.\",\"AI Gateway call failed: Free tier users do not have access to this model. Upgrade to paid credits at https://vercel.com/d?to=%2F%5Bteam%5D%2F%7E%2Fai%3Fmodal%3Dtop-up for unrestricted access.\"],\"drivers\":[\"Current-law CTC and EITC parameters\",\"Employment and earnings\",\"Housing and medical expense adjustments\",\"SNAP and other in-kind resources\"],\"source\":\"census_calibration_fallback\",\"generatedAt\":\"2026-06-23T15:21:11.105Z\",\"pointEstimate\":13,\"ciLow\":11.9,\"ciHigh\":14.3}\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/codex_stdout.jsonl:3:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"schemaVersion\\\":\\\"brier_reasoning_judge_v1\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Across the 8 reviewed CMS Medicaid ex parte renewal-share traces, Brier generally identified the correct state-row resolver, used official CMS/data.medicaid.gov context, anchored forecasts in state-specific recent history, and incorporated pre-submit reviewer feedback into more auditable prior/update/interval explanations. The main system weaknesses are repeated: catalog lookups sometimes expose prior point/interval values that exactly match the final forecast and create circularity risk; the strict first-print original-submission resolver repeatedly drifted into same-release-day correction exceptions before review; sparse historical samples were used without a structured representation of missing months, vintage status, and volatility method; and high-ceiling percentage targets need a more standardized bounded-interval calibration. These are fixable with prompt changes, validators, and CMS-specific source adapter fields rather than case-by-case reviewer intervention.\\\",\\\"reviewedRunCount\\\":8,\\\"strengths\\\":[\\\"Most traces correctly treated the target as a single state row rather than a national average.\\\",\\\"The runs consistently used CMS/data.medicaid.gov as the resolution source rather than relying on secondary mirrors.\\\",\\\"Reasoning usually named recent state-specific observations and used latest-value persistence or damped local trend as the baseline.\\\",\\\"Pre-submit review caught several concrete issues, and final traces often recorded accepted fixes in the review disposition.\\\",\\\"Several runs explicitly noted that 2026-12-15 is ledger-based because no future CMS placeholder was found, improving auditability of the schedule assumption.\\\",\\\"High-share states generally recognized the 100 percent mechanical ceiling and made intervals asymmetric or capped.\\\"],\\\"systemIssues\\\":[{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"catalog_prior_circularity\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"high\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Several traces fetched registered catalog point estimates and intervals that exactly matched the final forecast, making the reasoning appear circular even when later text claimed independent derivation.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"first_print_rule_drift\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"high\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"The first-print original-submission resolver repeatedly acquired same-release-day correction exceptions or ambiguous correction language that conflicted with the canonical ledger rule.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"sparse_history_unstructured\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"data_adapter\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Runs relied on sparse five-point historical samples but did not have a structured way to declare whether skipped months were unavailable, intentionally excluded, preliminary, original, or latest inspected.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"interval_calibration_is_judgmental\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Interval widths were often justified after the fact from sparse moves, missing-month uncertainty, and cohort risk without a consistent named calibration rule or volatility statistic.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"bounded_percent_targets_need_policy\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"pack\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"High-share percentage targets near 100 percent used ad hoc ceiling caps, commonly 99.0, without a standardized bounded-distribution or tail-mass convention.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"wrong_vintage_source_context\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"data_adapter\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Some source contexts included preliminary-status CMS URLs while the resolver required original O rows, forcing the reasoning to clarify that those links were only for release timing.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"reviewer_findings_repeat\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"The same reviewer findings recurred across runs, especially resolver correction exceptions, catalog circularity, and sparse interval explanations, indicating they should be enforced before pre-submit review.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]}],\\\"recommendations\\\":[{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"now\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Block same-day correction exceptions for strict first-print targets.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The resolution value must be mechanically reproducible. Allowing corrections within a release day creates cutoff and timezone ambiguity and repeatedly required reviewer correction.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add a validator rule for targets with resolutionRule containing first print, first publication, or original (O): reject reasoning or normalized cells whose resolutionRule includes phrases such as same release day, same-day correction, corrected before release day ends, or unless CMS corrects, unless the target ledger explicitly contains that exception.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Cleaner resolver text and fewer repeated pre-submit warnings on CMS first-print targets.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Some official datasets may publish corrected files under the same timestamp; those cases would need an explicit ledger flag rather than free-text exceptions.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"now\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Forbid using catalog point estimates and intervals as forecast evidence.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The forecast trace should be independently auditable. Showing prior catalog values that match the final output makes it unclear whether Brier reasoned or copied.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Amend the analyst prompt: catalog or ledger lookup may verify slug, unit, dataPointId, resolver, source, and resolution date only. If pointEstimate, ciLow, or ciHigh are present in local catalog context, ignore them and do not include them in tool results or reasoning unless explicitly auditing an existing catalog forecast.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Removes circular-looking traces and improves trust in generated forecasts.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"The model loses access to useful baselines from previous forecasts; if needed, expose them through a separate labeled comparison track, not the main forecast evidence track.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"now\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"data_adapter\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Add a CMS Medicaid PI history adapter that returns structured vintage-aware observations.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The fast public-release prompt is a reasonable match for CMS series, but the repeated sparse-history caveats show the agent lacks a clean history table with month coverage and submission status.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Implement an adapter output object with fields: state, reportingPeriod, value, numerator, denominator, submissionStatus, firstPrintObservedAt, sourceUrl, isMissingMonth, missingReason, and vintageType. Provide the last N monthly original/O observations plus explicit unavailable months to the analyst prompt.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Better trend and volatility estimates, fewer ambiguous statements about inspected samples, and easier audit of first-print versus preliminary values.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Requires adapter maintenance when CMS schema or datastore identifiers change.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"pack\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Create a bounded-percentage interval pack for shares near 0 or 100 percent.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Several high-share states used judgmental 99.0 caps. A standard method would improve calibration consistency and make tail treatment auditable.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add a pack that instructs Brier to model percentage shares on a logit or clipped-beta scale when point estimates are above 85 percent or below 15 percent, then transform back to percent and report whether bounds are distribution-derived or policy-capped.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"More coherent asymmetric intervals for Arizona, California, Connecticut, DC, and similar ceiling-constrained series.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"May over-formalize sparse administrative series if the transformed model is presented with false precision; prompt should require a plain-language caveat.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Require a structured prior-update-interval block with named components.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The reviewed traces improved after reviewer intervention, but many initial weaknesses were about unclear update sizes and interval mapping. Making the representation mandatory should reduce repeated warnings.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Require fields in reasoning: historyWindow, observationsUsed, missingObservationPolicy, priorAnchor, updateComponents with signed pp values, volatilityStatistic, intervalExpansionFactors, boundedTargetAdjustment, and finalArithmetic.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"More comparable traces across states and easier automated review of arbitrary judgmental adjustments.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Longer traces and possible boilerplate if the fast prompt overuses the structure on simple stable series.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Detect repeated reviewer findings and promote them to automatic checks.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Pre-submit review repeatedly caught the same classes of issues. These should be deterministic checks where possible, freeing review for substantive reasoning quality.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add reviewer-finding aggregation by rubricItem and phrase signature. When a warning appears in three or more recent runs for the same series family, open a validator suggestion or fail condition, starting with resolver exceptions, catalog prior references, and missing sample-size statements.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Reduces manual review churn and prevents known problems from recurring in batch runs.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Phrase-based detection can be brittle; use structured fields where available and keep the initial mode as warning-only before blocking.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"later\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"ui\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Show source vintage and missing-history coverage on forecast detail pages.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Readers need to distinguish official source evidence, local derived history, preliminary release timing links, and original-resolution rows.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add a compact evidence table on run detail pages with columns for source type, reporting period, submission status, value role, and whether it was used for target resolution, history, timing, or only target registration.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Improves auditability and makes circularity or wrong-vintage evidence easier to spot visually.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Adds UI density; keep it collapsed or grouped for long traces.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\"]}],\\\"promptPatchCandidates\\\":[{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add: For ledger/catalog lookups, use only target identity fields such as slug, unit, dataPointId, resolution source, resolution rule, and resolution date. Do not read, quote, or use existing catalog point estimates or intervals as evidence for a new forecast unless the task is explicitly to review an existing forecast.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add: For first-print or original-vintage targets, copy the ledger resolver exactly in substance. Do not add same-day correction, later correction, or release-day grace exceptions unless the registered target rule explicitly includes them.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add a required prior/update/interval section with: observations used, observations unavailable or skipped, prior anchor, signed update components, volatility statistic, interval expansion rationale, bounded-target adjustment, and final arithmetic.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add: When a source URL uses a different vintage, status, or filter from the resolver, label its role explicitly, for example release timing only, not historical value source or resolver evidence.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"CMS Medicaid PI prompt pack or source adapter prompt\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Expose a structured CMS history table for the requested state and measure, including reporting period, original/preliminary/updated status, numerator, denominator, computed share, first observed date, and missing-month reason. Instruct the analyst to prefer this table over ad hoc sparse catalog context.\\\"}]}\"}}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-runs.json:18:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-runs.json:40:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-runs.json:62:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-runs.json:84:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-runs.json:106:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-runs.json:128:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-runs.json:150:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-runs.json:172:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/judge.json:10:    \"Several runs explicitly noted that 2026-12-15 is ledger-based because no future CMS placeholder was found, improving auditability of the schedule assumption.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-38-10z-reasoning-judge/judge.json:3:  \"summary\": \"Across the six traces, Brier usually found official sources, named the resolving series, incorporated pre-submit review findings, and converted draft weaknesses into clearer resolver language, explicit priors, and interval math. The repeated weakness is that fast public-release runs often repair missing structure late in the trace with judgmental assumptions rather than fetching or representing the most relevant historical sequence, release calendar, or formula inputs in a reusable way. Several targets are mechanically resolvable but differ in character: some are public-release nowcasts needing source adapters and scheduled release metadata, while the CTC target is closer to a statutory formula nowcast and should be handled by a strategy/formula pack rather than the generic fast prompt alone.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-38-10z-reasoning-judge/codex_stdout.jsonl:3:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\\"schemaVersion\\\":\\\"brier_reasoning_judge_v1\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Across the six traces, Brier usually found official sources, named the resolving series, incorporated pre-submit review findings, and converted draft weaknesses into clearer resolver language, explicit priors, and interval math. The repeated weakness is that fast public-release runs often repair missing structure late in the trace with judgmental assumptions rather than fetching or representing the most relevant historical sequence, release calendar, or formula inputs in a reusable way. Several targets are mechanically resolvable but differ in character: some are public-release nowcasts needing source adapters and scheduled release metadata, while the CTC target is closer to a statutory formula nowcast and should be handled by a strategy/formula pack rather than the generic fast prompt alone.\\\",\\\"reviewedRunCount\\\":6,\\\"strengths\\\":[\\\"All six runs use official or near-official source families for the final resolver rather than news or secondary summaries.\\\",\\\"Pre-submit review is materially useful: blocking resolver, prior, and interval findings are reflected in the final reasoning for every run.\\\",\\\"Most final traces distinguish the target from nearby lookalikes, such as MTS refunds versus IRS filing-season refunds, CTC maximum versus refundable portion, and ONS LFS unemployment versus payroll or claimant-count indicators.\\\",\\\"Several runs include transparent arithmetic for the point estimate and interval, making audit failures easier to diagnose.\\\",\\\"The ONS, SNAP, IRS refunds, and MTS traces correctly use release timing or first-print concepts rather than later revised values.\\\"],\\\"systemIssues\\\":[{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"historical_sequence_not_structured\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"high\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Runs frequently acknowledge the need for recent same-series history but either do not fetch a clean sequence or encode it only as prose, leaving priors and intervals partly judgmental.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\\\",\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\",\\\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"resolver_date_repairs_are_repeated\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"high\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Multiple drafts had resolver date/source problems that were caught only by review; the system should validate inferred cadence, placeholder URLs, and input-date versus resolving-publication mismatches before draft submission.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\",\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"formula_targets_need_separate_strategy\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"pack\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"The CTC target is dominated by statute, chained-CPI windows, and rounding thresholds, which does not fit the generic fast public-release forecasting pattern as well as a formula-nowcast strategy would.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"interval_calibration_afterthought\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Intervals are often justified after the fact with plausible but ad hoc assumptions rather than a standard interval object tied to observed volatility, revision error, sampling error, or discrete probability mass.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\\\",\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\",\\\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\\\",\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"prior_catalog_reconciliation_untyped\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"ui\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"When catalog priors or prior runs are used, the trace does not expose a structured prior-versus-update path; reconciliation appears as prose, making run comparison and audit harder.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\",\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"release_calendar_not_adapter_backed\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"data_adapter\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Release dates are sometimes verified manually in traces, but the same source families need reusable calendar adapters so the runner can distinguish official scheduled dates, expected windows, and unknown future first-print pages.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\\\",\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]}],\\\"recommendations\\\":[{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"now\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Add resolver-date/source validation for future first-print targets.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Several traces needed review to catch unsupported resolution dates, stale analogue URLs, or confusion between formula input dates and final resolving publications. Catching this before finalization improves auditability and reduces bad catalog metadata.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Require each cell to classify resolutionDate as official_scheduled_release, official_placeholder_release, policy_deadline, or unresolved_until_first_post. Reject or warn when the source URL is a prior-year analogue without a stable index/placeholder, or when the date source is an input release rather than the resolving publication.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Fewer cadence-inferred dates and fewer future targets wired to stale resolver URLs.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Some valid targets may lack official calendars and need explicit unresolved-until-first-post handling rather than a hard failure.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\",\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"now\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Require a structured prior/update/interval block in every forecast trace.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The traces often contain the right ingredients but mix them into prose. A structured representation would make weaknesses visible to validators, comparisons, and future packs.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add required fields or reasoning sections: modelPrior.value, modelPrior.method, historicalSample.values, adjustment.components, interval.method, interval.inputs, and interval.impliedBounds. Allow 'not fetched' only with a reason and a fallback uncertainty rule.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"More consistent priors and intervals, and easier detection of hand-waved adjustments.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Fast runs may take longer or produce more validation failures until adapters provide the needed history automatically.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\\\",\\\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"data_adapter\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Build official history adapters for repeated source families.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Medicaid, MTS, IRS filing statistics, ONS MGSX, SNAP COLA, and CPI-linked tax parameters recur and need consistent historical samples rather than one-off page reads.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Create adapters that return typed recent observations, first-print dates, units, revision/vintage flags, and source URLs for CMS Medicaid enrollment, Treasury MTS Table 4, IRS Filing Season Statistics, ONS time series, USDA FNS SNAP COLA tables, and BLS CPI/C-CPI-U release windows.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Better model priors, less manual arithmetic, and fewer source-selection mistakes.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Adapters can encode wrong table mappings if not tested against historical first prints.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\\\",\\\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\\\",\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"pack\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Add a formula-nowcast pack for statutory rounded-dollar targets.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The CTC run is mostly a threshold formula with discrete outcomes, not a generic trend forecast. A dedicated pack would push the agent to enumerate inputs, thresholds, remaining unknown months, and probability mass by rounded outcome.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Create a pack requiring: statutory base amount, indexing formula, base year, inflation window, observed input months, remaining input months, rounding rule, threshold table, and probability distribution over official rounded values.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Cleaner forecasts for tax parameters, benefit formulas, and other indexed statutory values.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Overconfidence if the pack treats legal interpretation as fixed when IRS implementation could differ.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"ui\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Show strategy-track updates separately from final prose reasoning.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Prior traces and catalog priors are useful but not structured enough to compare how a new run moved the forecast.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"In the UI and record schema, add a compact update table with rows for catalog prior, official latest level, model prior, inside-view adjustment, policy/formula adjustment, and final forecast. Store numeric deltas and cited evidence per row.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Reviewers can quickly see whether updates are evidence-backed or judgmental.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"May add clutter unless the UI keeps the table compact and collapsible.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\",\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"later\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"scheduler\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Route target types to specialized prompt modes instead of sending all through the fast public-release prompt.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Fast mode works for many official-release forecasts but is less suitable for formula thresholds, unresolved future placeholders, and targets requiring exact vintage handling.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add target metadata such as release_series, statutory_formula, vintage_revision, first_print_page, and survey_sampling. Use it to select public_release_fast, formula_nowcast, vintage_series, or survey_nowcast prompt modes.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Fewer mismatched reasoning templates and more relevant evidence collection.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Misclassification could send a simple target to an overly complex prompt.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\",\\\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]}],\\\"promptPatchCandidates\\\":[{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add a required 'Structured forecast basis' section before the final forecast: latest official level, historical sample, model prior, evidence-backed adjustments, interval method, and explicit unresolved data gaps.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add resolver instructions: do not use an input release date as resolutionDate when the target resolves to a later agency publication; classify the date basis and cite the official calendar, placeholder, policy deadline, or first-post fallback.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"For formula-driven targets, require a threshold table and discrete probability mass over rounded outcomes; do not force a continuous trend model when the statutory formula dominates.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"validators/forecast-cell validation surface\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Warn when reasoning says a same-series history was not fetched but the interval uses realized-volatility language; require either historicalSample values or an explicit fallback uncertainty model.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"validators/resolution metadata validation surface\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Flag resolver URLs that point to prior-year analogue pages for future first-print targets unless a stable index or future placeholder is also present.\\\"}]}\"}}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-16/2026-06-16t10-10-05z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-2026-q4/prompt.md:144:  released ~the 3rd Friday; schedule at\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-16/2026-06-16t12-33-11z-us-dol-initial-claims-sa-week-2026-06-13/prompt.md:85:- resolutionDate must be verified from an official release calendar or announcement schedule this run. Do not infer it from cadence.\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/codex_events.jsonl:3:{\"type\": \"item.completed\", \"item\": {\"id\": \"item_0\", \"type\": \"agent_message\", \"text\": \"{\\\"schemaVersion\\\":\\\"brier_reasoning_judge_v1\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Across the 8 reviewed CMS Medicaid ex parte renewal-share traces, Brier generally identified the correct state-row resolver, used official CMS/data.medicaid.gov context, anchored forecasts in state-specific recent history, and incorporated pre-submit reviewer feedback into more auditable prior/update/interval explanations. The main system weaknesses are repeated: catalog lookups sometimes expose prior point/interval values that exactly match the final forecast and create circularity risk; the strict first-print original-submission resolver repeatedly drifted into same-release-day correction exceptions before review; sparse historical samples were used without a structured representation of missing months, vintage status, and volatility method; and high-ceiling percentage targets need a more standardized bounded-interval calibration. These are fixable with prompt changes, validators, and CMS-specific source adapter fields rather than case-by-case reviewer intervention.\\\",\\\"reviewedRunCount\\\":8,\\\"strengths\\\":[\\\"Most traces correctly treated the target as a single state row rather than a national average.\\\",\\\"The runs consistently used CMS/data.medicaid.gov as the resolution source rather than relying on secondary mirrors.\\\",\\\"Reasoning usually named recent state-specific observations and used latest-value persistence or damped local trend as the baseline.\\\",\\\"Pre-submit review caught several concrete issues, and final traces often recorded accepted fixes in the review disposition.\\\",\\\"Several runs explicitly noted that 2026-12-15 is ledger-based because no future CMS placeholder was found, improving auditability of the schedule assumption.\\\",\\\"High-share states generally recognized the 100 percent mechanical ceiling and made intervals asymmetric or capped.\\\"],\\\"systemIssues\\\":[{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"catalog_prior_circularity\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"high\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Several traces fetched registered catalog point estimates and intervals that exactly matched the final forecast, making the reasoning appear circular even when later text claimed independent derivation.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"first_print_rule_drift\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"high\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"The first-print original-submission resolver repeatedly acquired same-release-day correction exceptions or ambiguous correction language that conflicted with the canonical ledger rule.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"sparse_history_unstructured\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"data_adapter\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Runs relied on sparse five-point historical samples but did not have a structured way to declare whether skipped months were unavailable, intentionally excluded, preliminary, original, or latest inspected.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"interval_calibration_is_judgmental\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Interval widths were often justified after the fact from sparse moves, missing-month uncertainty, and cohort risk without a consistent named calibration rule or volatility statistic.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"bounded_percent_targets_need_policy\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"pack\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"High-share percentage targets near 100 percent used ad hoc ceiling caps, commonly 99.0, without a standardized bounded-distribution or tail-mass convention.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"wrong_vintage_source_context\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"data_adapter\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Some source contexts included preliminary-status CMS URLs while the resolver required original O rows, forcing the reasoning to clarify that those links were only for release timing.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"reviewer_findings_repeat\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"The same reviewer findings recurred across runs, especially resolver correction exceptions, catalog circularity, and sparse interval explanations, indicating they should be enforced before pre-submit review.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]}],\\\"recommendations\\\":[{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"now\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Block same-day correction exceptions for strict first-print targets.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The resolution value must be mechanically reproducible. Allowing corrections within a release day creates cutoff and timezone ambiguity and repeatedly required reviewer correction.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add a validator rule for targets with resolutionRule containing first print, first publication, or original (O): reject reasoning or normalized cells whose resolutionRule includes phrases such as same release day, same-day correction, corrected before release day ends, or unless CMS corrects, unless the target ledger explicitly contains that exception.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Cleaner resolver text and fewer repeated pre-submit warnings on CMS first-print targets.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Some official datasets may publish corrected files under the same timestamp; those cases would need an explicit ledger flag rather than free-text exceptions.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"now\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Forbid using catalog point estimates and intervals as forecast evidence.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The forecast trace should be independently auditable. Showing prior catalog values that match the final output makes it unclear whether Brier reasoned or copied.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Amend the analyst prompt: catalog or ledger lookup may verify slug, unit, dataPointId, resolver, source, and resolution date only. If pointEstimate, ciLow, or ciHigh are present in local catalog context, ignore them and do not include them in tool results or reasoning unless explicitly auditing an existing catalog forecast.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Removes circular-looking traces and improves trust in generated forecasts.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"The model loses access to useful baselines from previous forecasts; if needed, expose them through a separate labeled comparison track, not the main forecast evidence track.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"now\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"data_adapter\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Add a CMS Medicaid PI history adapter that returns structured vintage-aware observations.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The fast public-release prompt is a reasonable match for CMS series, but the repeated sparse-history caveats show the agent lacks a clean history table with month coverage and submission status.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Implement an adapter output object with fields: state, reportingPeriod, value, numerator, denominator, submissionStatus, firstPrintObservedAt, sourceUrl, isMissingMonth, missingReason, and vintageType. Provide the last N monthly original/O observations plus explicit unavailable months to the analyst prompt.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Better trend and volatility estimates, fewer ambiguous statements about inspected samples, and easier audit of first-print versus preliminary values.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Requires adapter maintenance when CMS schema or datastore identifiers change.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"pack\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Create a bounded-percentage interval pack for shares near 0 or 100 percent.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Several high-share states used judgmental 99.0 caps. A standard method would improve calibration consistency and make tail treatment auditable.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add a pack that instructs Brier to model percentage shares on a logit or clipped-beta scale when point estimates are above 85 percent or below 15 percent, then transform back to percent and report whether bounds are distribution-derived or policy-capped.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"More coherent asymmetric intervals for Arizona, California, Connecticut, DC, and similar ceiling-constrained series.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"May over-formalize sparse administrative series if the transformed model is presented with false precision; prompt should require a plain-language caveat.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Require a structured prior-update-interval block with named components.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The reviewed traces improved after reviewer intervention, but many initial weaknesses were about unclear update sizes and interval mapping. Making the representation mandatory should reduce repeated warnings.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Require fields in reasoning: historyWindow, observationsUsed, missingObservationPolicy, priorAnchor, updateComponents with signed pp values, volatilityStatistic, intervalExpansionFactors, boundedTargetAdjustment, and finalArithmetic.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"More comparable traces across states and easier automated review of arbitrary judgmental adjustments.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Longer traces and possible boilerplate if the fast prompt overuses the structure on simple stable series.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Detect repeated reviewer findings and promote them to automatic checks.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Pre-submit review repeatedly caught the same classes of issues. These should be deterministic checks where possible, freeing review for substantive reasoning quality.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add reviewer-finding aggregation by rubricItem and phrase signature. When a warning appears in three or more recent runs for the same series family, open a validator suggestion or fail condition, starting with resolver exceptions, catalog prior references, and missing sample-size statements.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Reduces manual review churn and prevents known problems from recurring in batch runs.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Phrase-based detection can be brittle; use structured fields where available and keep the initial mode as warning-only before blocking.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"later\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"ui\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Show source vintage and missing-history coverage on forecast detail pages.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Readers need to distinguish official source evidence, local derived history, preliminary release timing links, and original-resolution rows.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add a compact evidence table on run detail pages with columns for source type, reporting period, submission status, value role, and whether it was used for target resolution, history, timing, or only target registration.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Improves auditability and makes circularity or wrong-vintage evidence easier to spot visually.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Adds UI density; keep it collapsed or grouped for long traces.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\\\",\\\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\\\"]}],\\\"promptPatchCandidates\\\":[{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add: For ledger/catalog lookups, use only target identity fields such as slug, unit, dataPointId, resolution source, resolution rule, and resolution date. Do not read, quote, or use existing catalog point estimates or intervals as evidence for a new forecast unless the task is explicitly to review an existing forecast.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add: For first-print or original-vintage targets, copy the ledger resolver exactly in substance. Do not add same-day correction, later correction, or release-day grace exceptions unless the registered target rule explicitly includes them.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add a required prior/update/interval section with: observations used, observations unavailable or skipped, prior anchor, signed update components, volatility statistic, interval expansion rationale, bounded-target adjustment, and final arithmetic.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add: When a source URL uses a different vintage, status, or filter from the resolver, label its role explicitly, for example release timing only, not historical value source or resolver evidence.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"CMS Medicaid PI prompt pack or source adapter prompt\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Expose a structured CMS history table for the requested state and measure, including reporting period, original/preliminary/updated status, numerator, denominator, computed share, first observed date, and missing-month reason. Instruct the analyst to prefer this table over ad hoc sparse catalog context.\\\"}]}\"}}\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-38-10z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:411:        \"call\": \"Checked the Fiscal Data release calendar page for the September 2026 MTS release schedule and the MTS publication timing note in official MTS PDFs.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-38-10z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:412:        \"result\": \"Fetched official Fiscal Data release calendar surface showing Release Calendar, copyright 2026, and the upcoming-data-release schedule; September 2026 Monthly Treasury Statement is scheduled for 2026-10-20, and MTS PDFs state the statement is normally released on the 8th workday after the reporting month.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-38-10z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:717:        \"result\": \"Fetched release schedule: Consumer Price Index for August 2026 is scheduled for September 11, 2026 at 08:30 AM Eastern; this fixes the last month in the September 2025-August 2026 CPI window used for calendar-year 2027 tax inflation adjustments, but the resolving source remains the later IRS first-print tax-year 2027 inflation-adjustment publication.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:57:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:70:    \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:97:        \"result\": \"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak, unit percent, registered catalog resolutionDate 2026-12-15, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ak.aug_2026.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:145:        \"text\": \"Resolution-date note: the target ledger provides 2026-12-15 for this August 2026 CMS fixed-vintage row, while the official CMS public pages checked through the local run record establish the monthly data.Medicaid.gov release vehicle but did not expose a separate future dated placeholder for this exact August 2026 state row. I keep the forecast tied to the canonical ledger target and bind resolution to the first official CMS dataset print.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:202:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:215:    \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:216:    \"resolutionRule\": \"Resolve to Alabama's August 2026 reporting-period original first-publication state row in the CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data on data.medicaid.gov. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published ex parte renewal count divided by the published completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS print available through the dataset; ignore later updated submissions or revisions. The registered ledger resolution date is 2026-12-15; I did not find a future-dated CMS release-calendar placeholder in this fast run, so this remains tied to the canonical target while the reasoning notes the schedule evidence limitation.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:261:        \"result\": \"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al, unit percent, registered catalog resolutionDate 2026-12-15, prior point 57.1, prior 80% interval 51.9 to 62.2, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.al.aug_2026.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:283:        \"text\": \"Counter-consideration: upside outside the interval would require a sustained automation or data-match improvement pushing Alabama above roughly 62 percent. Downside outside the interval would require a manual-heavy renewal cohort, data-source outage, or operational regression pushing the share below roughly 52 percent. A schedule counter-consideration is that CMS publishes this series monthly but I did not verify a CMS page explicitly naming 2026-12-15 for the August 2026 first print.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:326:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:339:    \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:366:        \"result\": \"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar, unit percent, registered resolutionDate 2026-12-15, point 89.8, 80% interval 85.6 to 93.9, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ar.aug_2026.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:384:        \"result\": \"Fetched ledger resolutionDate 2026-12-15; prior CMS monthly page evidence showed Preliminary March 2026 data Last Updated June 26, 2026 and data.Medicaid.gov monthly update behavior, while no separate future CMS placeholder for the exact August 2026 Arkansas row was exposed in the checked context.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:408:        \"text\": \"Resolution-date note: the canonical ledger target uses 2026-12-15. The checked CMS release context supports the official data.Medicaid.gov monthly release vehicle but did not expose a separate future dated August 2026 Arkansas placeholder, so I keep the forecast tied to the ledger target and bind resolution to the first official CMS dataset print.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:412:        \"text\": \"Review disposition: accepted the resolver fix by removing the release-day correction exception, made the interval construction more explicit, split the +0.7 pp update into persistence-dominant components, and added the five-point sample size, center, and range. Kept the canonical 2026-12-15 resolutionDate because no exact future CMS placeholder was found in the checked context.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:452:          \"summary\": \"Keep the canonical resolutionDate of 2026-12-15, but mention that it is ledger-based because no exact future CMS placeholder was found.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:471:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:484:    \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:485:    \"resolutionRule\": \"Resolve to Arizona's August 2026 reporting-period original (O) state row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c when CMS first publishes that row. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published count of completed renewals processed through the ex parte process divided by the published total completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS print available on data.medicaid.gov; ignore later updated submissions or revisions unless CMS corrects the original row before the same release day ends. The official Medicaid.gov monthly reports page verifies that data.Medicaid.gov is updated monthly and showed the latest current release, Preliminary March 2026, last updated June 26, 2026; I did not find a future dated official August 2026 placeholder, so this remains tied to the canonical ledger resolutionDate 2026-12-15.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:510:        \"result\": \"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az, unit percent, registered catalog resolutionDate 2026-12-15, prior catalog point 93.3, prior 80% interval 85.9 to 99.0, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.az.aug_2026.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:558:        \"text\": \"Resolution-date note: the official CMS page verified the monthly release vehicle and current June 26, 2026 update, but did not expose a future dated August 2026 state-row placeholder. I keep the forecast tied to the canonical ledger date 2026-12-15 and bind resolution to the first official CMS dataset print.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:621:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:634:    \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:635:    \"resolutionRule\": \"Resolve to California's August 2026 reporting-period original (O) state row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c when CMS first publishes that row. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published count of completed renewals processed through the ex parte process divided by the published total completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS original-submission print available on data.medicaid.gov; ignore later updated submissions or revisions. The Medicaid.gov monthly reports page verifies the monthly release vehicle and showed current release evidence; I found no public future-dated August 2026 placeholder, so this remains tied to the canonical ledger resolutionDate 2026-12-15.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:662:        \"result\": \"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca, unit percent, registered catalog resolutionDate 2026-12-15, prior catalog point 88.9, prior 80% interval 78.6 to 99.0, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ca.aug_2026.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:710:        \"text\": \"Resolution-date note: the official Medicaid.gov page verified the monthly release vehicle and current June 26, 2026 update cycle, but did not expose a future dated August 2026 state-row placeholder. I keep the forecast tied to the canonical ledger date 2026-12-15 and bind resolution to the first official CMS original-submission dataset print.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:754:          \"summary\": \"Mention that the 2026-12-15 date is the ledger resolution date despite no future CMS placeholder being found.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:773:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:786:    \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:787:    \"resolutionRule\": \"Resolve to Colorado's August 2026 reporting-period original (O) state row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c when CMS first publishes that row. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published count of completed renewals processed through the ex parte process divided by the published total completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS publication of the original O row on data.medicaid.gov and ignore later updated submissions or revisions. The checked Medicaid.gov release page verifies the monthly release vehicle and showed March 2026 preliminary data last updated June 26, 2026; I did not find a future dated official August 2026 placeholder, so this remains tied to the canonical ledger resolutionDate 2026-12-15.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:826:        \"result\": \"Fetched target registration values: canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co, unit percent, registered resolutionDate 2026-12-15, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.co.aug_2026. These were used only to confirm target identity, not to set the forecast.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:866:        \"text\": \"Resolution-date note: the official CMS page verified the monthly release vehicle and the June 26, 2026 current update, but did not expose a future dated August 2026 state-row placeholder during this fast run. I keep the forecast tied to the canonical ledger date 2026-12-15 and bind resolution to the first official CMS dataset print.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:917:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:930:    \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:931:    \"resolutionRule\": \"Resolve to Connecticut's August 2026 reporting-period original (O) state row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c when CMS first publishes that row. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published count of completed renewals processed through ex parte renewal divided by the published total completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS print available on data.medicaid.gov; ignore later updated submissions, revisions, or corrections. The official Medicaid.gov monthly reports page verifies the monthly release vehicle; I did not find a public future-dated August 2026 placeholder in the inspected context, so this remains tied to the canonical ledger resolutionDate 2026-12-15.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:958:        \"result\": \"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct, unit percent, registered catalog resolutionDate 2026-12-15, prior catalog point 96.8, prior 80% interval 93.0 to 99.0, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ct.aug_2026.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:1006:        \"text\": \"Resolution-date note: the official CMS page evidence supports the monthly release vehicle and the June 26, 2026 current update cycle, but the inspected context did not expose a future dated August 2026 state-row placeholder. I keep the forecast tied to the canonical ledger date 2026-12-15 and bind resolution to the first official CMS dataset print.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:1051:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:1064:    \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:1065:    \"resolutionRule\": \"Resolve to District of Columbia's August 2026 reporting-period original (O) state row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c exactly as first officially published on data.medicaid.gov. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published count of completed renewals processed through ex parte renewal divided by the published total completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Ignore later updated submissions or revisions. The official Medicaid.gov monthly reports page verifies the monthly release vehicle; I did not find a public future-dated August 2026 placeholder in the inspected context, so this remains tied to the canonical ledger resolutionDate 2026-12-15.\",\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:1092:        \"result\": \"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc, unit percent, registered catalog resolutionDate 2026-12-15, prior catalog point 98.0, prior 80% interval 91.6 to 99.0, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.dc.aug_2026.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/prompt.md:1140:        \"text\": \"Resolution-date note: the official CMS page evidence supports the monthly release vehicle and the June 26, 2026 current update cycle, but the inspected context did not expose a future dated August 2026 state-row placeholder. I keep the forecast tied to the canonical ledger date 2026-12-15 and bind resolution to the first official CMS dataset print.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-38-10z-reasoning-judge/codex_events.jsonl:3:{\"type\": \"item.completed\", \"item\": {\"id\": \"item_0\", \"type\": \"agent_message\", \"text\": \"{\\\"schemaVersion\\\":\\\"brier_reasoning_judge_v1\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Across the six traces, Brier usually found official sources, named the resolving series, incorporated pre-submit review findings, and converted draft weaknesses into clearer resolver language, explicit priors, and interval math. The repeated weakness is that fast public-release runs often repair missing structure late in the trace with judgmental assumptions rather than fetching or representing the most relevant historical sequence, release calendar, or formula inputs in a reusable way. Several targets are mechanically resolvable but differ in character: some are public-release nowcasts needing source adapters and scheduled release metadata, while the CTC target is closer to a statutory formula nowcast and should be handled by a strategy/formula pack rather than the generic fast prompt alone.\\\",\\\"reviewedRunCount\\\":6,\\\"strengths\\\":[\\\"All six runs use official or near-official source families for the final resolver rather than news or secondary summaries.\\\",\\\"Pre-submit review is materially useful: blocking resolver, prior, and interval findings are reflected in the final reasoning for every run.\\\",\\\"Most final traces distinguish the target from nearby lookalikes, such as MTS refunds versus IRS filing-season refunds, CTC maximum versus refundable portion, and ONS LFS unemployment versus payroll or claimant-count indicators.\\\",\\\"Several runs include transparent arithmetic for the point estimate and interval, making audit failures easier to diagnose.\\\",\\\"The ONS, SNAP, IRS refunds, and MTS traces correctly use release timing or first-print concepts rather than later revised values.\\\"],\\\"systemIssues\\\":[{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"historical_sequence_not_structured\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"high\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Runs frequently acknowledge the need for recent same-series history but either do not fetch a clean sequence or encode it only as prose, leaving priors and intervals partly judgmental.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\\\",\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\",\\\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"resolver_date_repairs_are_repeated\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"high\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Multiple drafts had resolver date/source problems that were caught only by review; the system should validate inferred cadence, placeholder URLs, and input-date versus resolving-publication mismatches before draft submission.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\",\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"formula_targets_need_separate_strategy\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"pack\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"The CTC target is dominated by statute, chained-CPI windows, and rounding thresholds, which does not fit the generic fast public-release forecasting pattern as well as a formula-nowcast strategy would.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"interval_calibration_afterthought\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Intervals are often justified after the fact with plausible but ad hoc assumptions rather than a standard interval object tied to observed volatility, revision error, sampling error, or discrete probability mass.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\\\",\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\",\\\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\\\",\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"prior_catalog_reconciliation_untyped\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"ui\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"When catalog priors or prior runs are used, the trace does not expose a structured prior-versus-update path; reconciliation appears as prose, making run comparison and audit harder.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\",\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\"]},{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"release_calendar_not_adapter_backed\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"medium\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"data_adapter\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Release dates are sometimes verified manually in traces, but the same source families need reusable calendar adapters so the runner can distinguish official scheduled dates, expected windows, and unknown future first-print pages.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\\\",\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]}],\\\"recommendations\\\":[{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"now\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"validator\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Add resolver-date/source validation for future first-print targets.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Several traces needed review to catch unsupported resolution dates, stale analogue URLs, or confusion between formula input dates and final resolving publications. Catching this before finalization improves auditability and reduces bad catalog metadata.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Require each cell to classify resolutionDate as official_scheduled_release, official_placeholder_release, policy_deadline, or unresolved_until_first_post. Reject or warn when the source URL is a prior-year analogue without a stable index/placeholder, or when the date source is an input release rather than the resolving publication.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Fewer cadence-inferred dates and fewer future targets wired to stale resolver URLs.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Some valid targets may lack official calendars and need explicit unresolved-until-first-post handling rather than a hard failure.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\",\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"now\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"prompt\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Require a structured prior/update/interval block in every forecast trace.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The traces often contain the right ingredients but mix them into prose. A structured representation would make weaknesses visible to validators, comparisons, and future packs.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add required fields or reasoning sections: modelPrior.value, modelPrior.method, historicalSample.values, adjustment.components, interval.method, interval.inputs, and interval.impliedBounds. Allow 'not fetched' only with a reason and a fallback uncertainty rule.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"More consistent priors and intervals, and easier detection of hand-waved adjustments.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Fast runs may take longer or produce more validation failures until adapters provide the needed history automatically.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\\\",\\\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"data_adapter\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Build official history adapters for repeated source families.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Medicaid, MTS, IRS filing statistics, ONS MGSX, SNAP COLA, and CPI-linked tax parameters recur and need consistent historical samples rather than one-off page reads.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Create adapters that return typed recent observations, first-print dates, units, revision/vintage flags, and source URLs for CMS Medicaid enrollment, Treasury MTS Table 4, IRS Filing Season Statistics, ONS time series, USDA FNS SNAP COLA tables, and BLS CPI/C-CPI-U release windows.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Better model priors, less manual arithmetic, and fewer source-selection mistakes.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Adapters can encode wrong table mappings if not tested against historical first prints.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\\\",\\\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\\\",\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"pack\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Add a formula-nowcast pack for statutory rounded-dollar targets.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The CTC run is mostly a threshold formula with discrete outcomes, not a generic trend forecast. A dedicated pack would push the agent to enumerate inputs, thresholds, remaining unknown months, and probability mass by rounded outcome.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Create a pack requiring: statutory base amount, indexing formula, base year, inflation window, observed input months, remaining input months, rounding rule, threshold table, and probability distribution over official rounded values.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Cleaner forecasts for tax parameters, benefit formulas, and other indexed statutory values.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Overconfidence if the pack treats legal interpretation as fixed when IRS implementation could differ.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"next\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"ui\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Show strategy-track updates separately from final prose reasoning.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Prior traces and catalog priors are useful but not structured enough to compare how a new run moved the forecast.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"In the UI and record schema, add a compact update table with rows for catalog prior, official latest level, model prior, inside-view adjustment, policy/formula adjustment, and final forecast. Store numeric deltas and cited evidence per row.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Reviewers can quickly see whether updates are evidence-backed or judgmental.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"May add clutter unless the UI keeps the table compact and collapsible.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\\\",\\\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\\\",\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\"]},{\\\"priority\\\":\\\"later\\\",\\\"area\\\":\\\"scheduler\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Route target types to specialized prompt modes instead of sending all through the fast public-release prompt.\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Fast mode works for many official-release forecasts but is less suitable for formula thresholds, unresolved future placeholders, and targets requiring exact vintage handling.\\\",\\\"proposedChange\\\":\\\"Add target metadata such as release_series, statutory_formula, vintage_revision, first_print_page, and survey_sampling. Use it to select public_release_fast, formula_nowcast, vintage_series, or survey_nowcast prompt modes.\\\",\\\"expectedImpact\\\":\\\"Fewer mismatched reasoning templates and more relevant evidence collection.\\\",\\\"risk\\\":\\\"Misclassification could send a simple target to an overly complex prompt.\\\",\\\"evidenceRunSlugs\\\":[\\\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\\\",\\\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\\\",\\\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\\\"]}],\\\"promptPatchCandidates\\\":[{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add a required 'Structured forecast basis' section before the final forecast: latest official level, historical sample, model prior, evidence-backed adjustments, interval method, and explicit unresolved data gaps.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Add resolver instructions: do not use an input release date as resolutionDate when the target resolves to a later agency publication; classify the date basis and cite the official calendar, placeholder, policy deadline, or first-post fallback.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"For formula-driven targets, require a threshold table and discrete probability mass over rounded outcomes; do not force a continuous trend model when the statutory formula dominates.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"validators/forecast-cell validation surface\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Warn when reasoning says a same-series history was not fetched but the interval uses realized-volatility language; require either historicalSample values or an explicit fallback uncertainty model.\\\"},{\\\"file\\\":\\\"validators/resolution metadata validation surface\\\",\\\"patchSummary\\\":\\\"Flag resolver URLs that point to prior-year analogue pages for future first-print targets unless a stable index or future placeholder is also present.\\\"}]}\"}}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-01/2026-07-01t05-12-15z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ky-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/normalized_cells.json:13:  \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-01/2026-07-01t05-12-15z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ky-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/normalized_cells.json:72:    \"result\": \"Fetched CMS dataset id 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c and datastore id 6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360; the target uses original submission status O, August 2026 reporting period, and a first-print resolution date of 2026-12-15 in the canonical ledger.\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-01/2026-07-01t05-12-15z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ky-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/normalized_cells.json:108:    \"text\": \"Resolution-date note: the official CMS page verifies the monthly public data.Medicaid.gov release vehicle and current update pattern, while the canonical ledger target supplies 2026-12-15 for this August 2026 fixed-vintage row. I did not find a separate CMS future-dated placeholder for the exact Kentucky August 2026 row, so the forecast remains tied to the ledger date and resolves on the first official CMS dataset print.\"\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-17-43z-reasoning-judge/stdout.txt:1:{\"schemaVersion\":\"brier_reasoning_judge_v1\",\"summary\":\"Across the 8 reviewed CMS Medicaid ex parte renewal-share traces, Brier generally identified the correct state-row resolver, used official CMS/data.medicaid.gov context, anchored forecasts in state-specific recent history, and incorporated pre-submit reviewer feedback into more auditable prior/update/interval explanations. The main system weaknesses are repeated: catalog lookups sometimes expose prior point/interval values that exactly match the final forecast and create circularity risk; the strict first-print original-submission resolver repeatedly drifted into same-release-day correction exceptions before review; sparse historical samples were used without a structured representation of missing months, vintage status, and volatility method; and high-ceiling percentage targets need a more standardized bounded-interval calibration. These are fixable with prompt changes, validators, and CMS-specific source adapter fields rather than case-by-case reviewer intervention.\",\"reviewedRunCount\":8,\"strengths\":[\"Most traces correctly treated the target as a single state row rather than a national average.\",\"The runs consistently used CMS/data.medicaid.gov as the resolution source rather than relying on secondary mirrors.\",\"Reasoning usually named recent state-specific observations and used latest-value persistence or damped local trend as the baseline.\",\"Pre-submit review caught several concrete issues, and final traces often recorded accepted fixes in the review disposition.\",\"Several runs explicitly noted that 2026-12-15 is ledger-based because no future CMS placeholder was found, improving auditability of the schedule assumption.\",\"High-share states generally recognized the 100 percent mechanical ceiling and made intervals asymmetric or capped.\"],\"systemIssues\":[{\"issueId\":\"catalog_prior_circularity\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Several traces fetched registered catalog point estimates and intervals that exactly matched the final forecast, making the reasoning appear circular even when later text claimed independent derivation.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"issueId\":\"first_print_rule_drift\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"area\":\"validator\",\"summary\":\"The first-print original-submission resolver repeatedly acquired same-release-day correction exceptions or ambiguous correction language that conflicted with the canonical ledger rule.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"issueId\":\"sparse_history_unstructured\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"data_adapter\",\"summary\":\"Runs relied on sparse five-point historical samples but did not have a structured way to declare whether skipped months were unavailable, intentionally excluded, preliminary, original, or latest inspected.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"issueId\":\"interval_calibration_is_judgmental\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Interval widths were often justified after the fact from sparse moves, missing-month uncertainty, and cohort risk without a consistent named calibration rule or volatility statistic.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"issueId\":\"bounded_percent_targets_need_policy\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"pack\",\"summary\":\"High-share percentage targets near 100 percent used ad hoc ceiling caps, commonly 99.0, without a standardized bounded-distribution or tail-mass convention.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"issueId\":\"wrong_vintage_source_context\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"data_adapter\",\"summary\":\"Some source contexts included preliminary-status CMS URLs while the resolver required original O rows, forcing the reasoning to clarify that those links were only for release timing.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\"]},{\"issueId\":\"reviewer_findings_repeat\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"validator\",\"summary\":\"The same reviewer findings recurred across runs, especially resolver correction exceptions, catalog circularity, and sparse interval explanations, indicating they should be enforced before pre-submit review.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]}],\"recommendations\":[{\"priority\":\"now\",\"area\":\"validator\",\"summary\":\"Block same-day correction exceptions for strict first-print targets.\",\"rationale\":\"The resolution value must be mechanically reproducible. Allowing corrections within a release day creates cutoff and timezone ambiguity and repeatedly required reviewer correction.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Add a validator rule for targets with resolutionRule containing first print, first publication, or original (O): reject reasoning or normalized cells whose resolutionRule includes phrases such as same release day, same-day correction, corrected before release day ends, or unless CMS corrects, unless the target ledger explicitly contains that exception.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Cleaner resolver text and fewer repeated pre-submit warnings on CMS first-print targets.\",\"risk\":\"Some official datasets may publish corrected files under the same timestamp; those cases would need an explicit ledger flag rather than free-text exceptions.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"now\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Forbid using catalog point estimates and intervals as forecast evidence.\",\"rationale\":\"The forecast trace should be independently auditable. Showing prior catalog values that match the final output makes it unclear whether Brier reasoned or copied.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Amend the analyst prompt: catalog or ledger lookup may verify slug, unit, dataPointId, resolver, source, and resolution date only. If pointEstimate, ciLow, or ciHigh are present in local catalog context, ignore them and do not include them in tool results or reasoning unless explicitly auditing an existing catalog forecast.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Removes circular-looking traces and improves trust in generated forecasts.\",\"risk\":\"The model loses access to useful baselines from previous forecasts; if needed, expose them through a separate labeled comparison track, not the main forecast evidence track.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"now\",\"area\":\"data_adapter\",\"summary\":\"Add a CMS Medicaid PI history adapter that returns structured vintage-aware observations.\",\"rationale\":\"The fast public-release prompt is a reasonable match for CMS series, but the repeated sparse-history caveats show the agent lacks a clean history table with month coverage and submission status.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Implement an adapter output object with fields: state, reportingPeriod, value, numerator, denominator, submissionStatus, firstPrintObservedAt, sourceUrl, isMissingMonth, missingReason, and vintageType. Provide the last N monthly original/O observations plus explicit unavailable months to the analyst prompt.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Better trend and volatility estimates, fewer ambiguous statements about inspected samples, and easier audit of first-print versus preliminary values.\",\"risk\":\"Requires adapter maintenance when CMS schema or datastore identifiers change.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-al\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"next\",\"area\":\"pack\",\"summary\":\"Create a bounded-percentage interval pack for shares near 0 or 100 percent.\",\"rationale\":\"Several high-share states used judgmental 99.0 caps. A standard method would improve calibration consistency and make tail treatment auditable.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Add a pack that instructs Brier to model percentage shares on a logit or clipped-beta scale when point estimates are above 85 percent or below 15 percent, then transform back to percent and report whether bounds are distribution-derived or policy-capped.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"More coherent asymmetric intervals for Arizona, California, Connecticut, DC, and similar ceiling-constrained series.\",\"risk\":\"May over-formalize sparse administrative series if the transformed model is presented with false precision; prompt should require a plain-language caveat.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ct\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"next\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Require a structured prior-update-interval block with named components.\",\"rationale\":\"The reviewed traces improved after reviewer intervention, but many initial weaknesses were about unclear update sizes and interval mapping. Making the representation mandatory should reduce repeated warnings.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Require fields in reasoning: historyWindow, observationsUsed, missingObservationPolicy, priorAnchor, updateComponents with signed pp values, volatilityStatistic, intervalExpansionFactors, boundedTargetAdjustment, and finalArithmetic.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"More comparable traces across states and easier automated review of arbitrary judgmental adjustments.\",\"risk\":\"Longer traces and possible boilerplate if the fast prompt overuses the structure on simple stable series.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"next\",\"area\":\"validator\",\"summary\":\"Detect repeated reviewer findings and promote them to automatic checks.\",\"rationale\":\"Pre-submit review repeatedly caught the same classes of issues. These should be deterministic checks where possible, freeing review for substantive reasoning quality.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Add reviewer-finding aggregation by rubricItem and phrase signature. When a warning appears in three or more recent runs for the same series family, open a validator suggestion or fail condition, starting with resolver exceptions, catalog prior references, and missing sample-size statements.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Reduces manual review churn and prevents known problems from recurring in batch runs.\",\"risk\":\"Phrase-based detection can be brittle; use structured fields where available and keep the initial mode as warning-only before blocking.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ak\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ar\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-dc\"]},{\"priority\":\"later\",\"area\":\"ui\",\"summary\":\"Show source vintage and missing-history coverage on forecast detail pages.\",\"rationale\":\"Readers need to distinguish official source evidence, local derived history, preliminary release timing links, and original-resolution rows.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Add a compact evidence table on run detail pages with columns for source type, reporting period, submission status, value role, and whether it was used for target resolution, history, timing, or only target registration.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Improves auditability and makes circularity or wrong-vintage evidence easier to spot visually.\",\"risk\":\"Adds UI density; keep it collapsed or grouped for long traces.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-az\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ca\",\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-co\"]}],\"promptPatchCandidates\":[{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"Add: For ledger/catalog lookups, use only target identity fields such as slug, unit, dataPointId, resolution source, resolution rule, and resolution date. Do not read, quote, or use existing catalog point estimates or intervals as evidence for a new forecast unless the task is explicitly to review an existing forecast.\"},{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"Add: For first-print or original-vintage targets, copy the ledger resolver exactly in substance. Do not add same-day correction, later correction, or release-day grace exceptions unless the registered target rule explicitly includes them.\"},{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"Add a required prior/update/interval section with: observations used, observations unavailable or skipped, prior anchor, signed update components, volatility statistic, interval expansion rationale, bounded-target adjustment, and final arithmetic.\"},{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"Add: When a source URL uses a different vintage, status, or filter from the resolver, label its role explicitly, for example release timing only, not historical value source or resolver evidence.\"},{\"file\":\"CMS Medicaid PI prompt pack or source adapter prompt\",\"patchSummary\":\"Expose a structured CMS history table for the requested state and measure, including reporting period, original/preliminary/updated status, numerator, denominator, computed share, first observed date, and missing-month reason. Instruct the analyst to prefer this table over ad hoc sparse catalog context.\"}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-targets.json:9:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-targets.json:20:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-targets.json:31:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-targets.json:42:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-targets.json:53:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-targets.json:64:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-targets.json:75:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-28-cms-ex-parte-wave-2-targets.json:86:      \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-31-57z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ga-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/manifest.json:11:    \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-27-cms-ex-parte-wave-1-runs-v2.json:18:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-27-cms-ex-parte-wave-1-runs-v2.json:39:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-27-cms-ex-parte-wave-1-runs-v2.json:60:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-27-cms-ex-parte-wave-1-runs-v2.json:81:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-27-cms-ex-parte-wave-1-runs-v2.json:102:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-27-cms-ex-parte-wave-1-runs-v2.json:123:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-27-cms-ex-parte-wave-1-runs-v2.json:144:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/batches/2026-06-27-cms-ex-parte-wave-1-runs-v2.json:165:        \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-16/2026-06-16t12-33-11z-us-dol-initial-claims-sa-week-2026-06-13/stdout.txt:1:{\"slug\":\"us-dol-initial-claims-sa-week-2026-06-13-first-print\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"US initial jobless claims, Jun. 13 week\",\"question\":\"U.S. Department of Labor Employment and Training Administration seasonally adjusted initial unemployment insurance claims for the week ending June 13, 2026, first print\",\"unit\":\"count\",\"pointEstimate\":225000,\"ciLow\":209000,\"ciHigh\":243000,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-06-18\",\"resolutionSource\":\"Official U.S. Department of Labor Employment and Training Administration Unemployment Insurance Weekly Claims release\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://www.dol.gov/ui/data.pdf\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to the advance seasonally adjusted initial claims figure for the week ending June 13, 2026 in the first official DOL Unemployment Insurance Weekly Claims release dated June 18, 2026. Use the initially printed value in persons; ignore later revisions or FRED backfills.\",\"dataPointId\":\"dol.ui.initial_claims.sa.2026-06-13.first_print\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"2026-06-06 latest SA initial claims\",\"value\":229000},{\"label\":\"2026-05-30 SA initial claims\",\"value\":225000},{\"label\":\"2026-05-23 SA initial claims\",\"value\":212000},{\"label\":\"2026-05-16 SA initial claims\",\"value\":210000},{\"label\":\"2026-06-06 four-week moving average\",\"value\":219000}],\"drivers\":[\"latest print rose to 229000\",\"four-week average at 219000\",\"prior week was 225000\",\"same-week 2025 level was 243000\",\"recent May-to-June prints remain in low-200000s range\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://oui.doleta.gov/unemploy/claims_arch.asp\",\"https://www.dol.gov/ui/data.pdf\",\"https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/ICSA\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-16T12:33:22Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for DOL initial claims, week ending June 13, 2026\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is the first official DOL ETA Unemployment Insurance Weekly Claims advance seasonally adjusted initial claims figure for the week-ending date June 13, 2026, not any later revised history.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the DOL ETA weekly claims archive and publication schedule page.\",\"result\":\"Official schedule says the UI Weekly Claims News Release is published each week on Thursday morning at 8:30 AM EST, lists 1 exception date in 2026, Wednesday November 25, 2026, and the page was updated June 11, 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the current official DOL UI Weekly Claims PDF release dated June 11, 2026.\",\"result\":\"For week ending June 6, 2026, seasonally adjusted initial claims were 229000, up 4000 from the prior unrevised 225000; the four-week moving average was 219000, up 4250.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Read the DOL release table for recent and prior-year claims context.\",\"result\":\"The DOL table shows SA initial claims of 229000 for June 6, 2026, 225000 for May 30, 2026, 212000 for May 23, 2026, and 246000 for the comparable prior-year week.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"history.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened FRED ICSA as a history mirror for the same ETA source series.\",\"result\":\"FRED showed 2026-06-06 at 229000, 2026-05-30 at 225000, 2026-05-23 at 212000, 2026-05-16 at 210000, 2026-05-09 at 212000, and next release date Jun 18, 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference class: for weekly initial claims, the near-term reference class is adjacent weekly prints around the latest release; the last five fetched SA observations are 212000, 210000, 212000, 225000, and 229000, while the official four-week average is 219000.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Blend latest level 229000, prior week 225000, and four-week average 219000 with more weight on persistence: 0.40*229000 + 0.35*225000 + 0.25*219000 = 225100, rounded to the nearest 1000 gives 225000. Set an 80% interval of roughly +/-16000 around the rounded point, giving 209000 to 243000.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: the latest unadjusted claims rose sharply by 39713 to 228276, and seasonal adjustment expected a large increase of 35595, so a second high print is plausible; however, the SA series often mean-reverts after jumps and the latest 229000 is already above the 219000 four-week average.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":225000,\"ciLow\":209000,\"ciHigh\":243000}]}\nrecords/brier-judges/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t23-38-10z-reasoning-judge/stdout.txt:1:{\"schemaVersion\":\"brier_reasoning_judge_v1\",\"summary\":\"Across the six traces, Brier usually found official sources, named the resolving series, incorporated pre-submit review findings, and converted draft weaknesses into clearer resolver language, explicit priors, and interval math. The repeated weakness is that fast public-release runs often repair missing structure late in the trace with judgmental assumptions rather than fetching or representing the most relevant historical sequence, release calendar, or formula inputs in a reusable way. Several targets are mechanically resolvable but differ in character: some are public-release nowcasts needing source adapters and scheduled release metadata, while the CTC target is closer to a statutory formula nowcast and should be handled by a strategy/formula pack rather than the generic fast prompt alone.\",\"reviewedRunCount\":6,\"strengths\":[\"All six runs use official or near-official source families for the final resolver rather than news or secondary summaries.\",\"Pre-submit review is materially useful: blocking resolver, prior, and interval findings are reflected in the final reasoning for every run.\",\"Most final traces distinguish the target from nearby lookalikes, such as MTS refunds versus IRS filing-season refunds, CTC maximum versus refundable portion, and ONS LFS unemployment versus payroll or claimant-count indicators.\",\"Several runs include transparent arithmetic for the point estimate and interval, making audit failures easier to diagnose.\",\"The ONS, SNAP, IRS refunds, and MTS traces correctly use release timing or first-print concepts rather than later revised values.\"],\"systemIssues\":[{\"issueId\":\"historical_sequence_not_structured\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Runs frequently acknowledge the need for recent same-series history but either do not fetch a clean sequence or encode it only as prose, leaving priors and intervals partly judgmental.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\",\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\",\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\",\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\"]},{\"issueId\":\"resolver_date_repairs_are_repeated\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"area\":\"validator\",\"summary\":\"Multiple drafts had resolver date/source problems that were caught only by review; the system should validate inferred cadence, placeholder URLs, and input-date versus resolving-publication mismatches before draft submission.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\",\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\",\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\"]},{\"issueId\":\"formula_targets_need_separate_strategy\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"pack\",\"summary\":\"The CTC target is dominated by statute, chained-CPI windows, and rounding thresholds, which does not fit the generic fast public-release forecasting pattern as well as a formula-nowcast strategy would.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\"]},{\"issueId\":\"interval_calibration_afterthought\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Intervals are often justified after the fact with plausible but ad hoc assumptions rather than a standard interval object tied to observed volatility, revision error, sampling error, or discrete probability mass.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\",\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\",\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\",\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\",\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\",\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\"]},{\"issueId\":\"prior_catalog_reconciliation_untyped\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"ui\",\"summary\":\"When catalog priors or prior runs are used, the trace does not expose a structured prior-versus-update path; reconciliation appears as prose, making run comparison and audit harder.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\",\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\",\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\"]},{\"issueId\":\"release_calendar_not_adapter_backed\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"area\":\"data_adapter\",\"summary\":\"Release dates are sometimes verified manually in traces, but the same source families need reusable calendar adapters so the runner can distinguish official scheduled dates, expected windows, and unknown future first-print pages.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\",\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\",\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\",\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\"]}],\"recommendations\":[{\"priority\":\"now\",\"area\":\"validator\",\"summary\":\"Add resolver-date/source validation for future first-print targets.\",\"rationale\":\"Several traces needed review to catch unsupported resolution dates, stale analogue URLs, or confusion between formula input dates and final resolving publications. Catching this before finalization improves auditability and reduces bad catalog metadata.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Require each cell to classify resolutionDate as official_scheduled_release, official_placeholder_release, policy_deadline, or unresolved_until_first_post. Reject or warn when the source URL is a prior-year analogue without a stable index/placeholder, or when the date source is an input release rather than the resolving publication.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Fewer cadence-inferred dates and fewer future targets wired to stale resolver URLs.\",\"risk\":\"Some valid targets may lack official calendars and need explicit unresolved-until-first-post handling rather than a hard failure.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\",\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\",\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\"]},{\"priority\":\"now\",\"area\":\"prompt\",\"summary\":\"Require a structured prior/update/interval block in every forecast trace.\",\"rationale\":\"The traces often contain the right ingredients but mix them into prose. A structured representation would make weaknesses visible to validators, comparisons, and future packs.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Add required fields or reasoning sections: modelPrior.value, modelPrior.method, historicalSample.values, adjustment.components, interval.method, interval.inputs, and interval.impliedBounds. Allow 'not fetched' only with a reason and a fallback uncertainty rule.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"More consistent priors and intervals, and easier detection of hand-waved adjustments.\",\"risk\":\"Fast runs may take longer or produce more validation failures until adapters provide the needed history automatically.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\",\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\",\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\"]},{\"priority\":\"next\",\"area\":\"data_adapter\",\"summary\":\"Build official history adapters for repeated source families.\",\"rationale\":\"Medicaid, MTS, IRS filing statistics, ONS MGSX, SNAP COLA, and CPI-linked tax parameters recur and need consistent historical samples rather than one-off page reads.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Create adapters that return typed recent observations, first-print dates, units, revision/vintage flags, and source URLs for CMS Medicaid enrollment, Treasury MTS Table 4, IRS Filing Season Statistics, ONS time series, USDA FNS SNAP COLA tables, and BLS CPI/C-CPI-U release windows.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Better model priors, less manual arithmetic, and fewer source-selection mistakes.\",\"risk\":\"Adapters can encode wrong table mappings if not tested against historical first prints.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\",\"individual-income-tax-refunds-fy2026\",\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\",\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\"]},{\"priority\":\"next\",\"area\":\"pack\",\"summary\":\"Add a formula-nowcast pack for statutory rounded-dollar targets.\",\"rationale\":\"The CTC run is mostly a threshold formula with discrete outcomes, not a generic trend forecast. A dedicated pack would push the agent to enumerate inputs, thresholds, remaining unknown months, and probability mass by rounded outcome.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Create a pack requiring: statutory base amount, indexing formula, base year, inflation window, observed input months, remaining input months, rounding rule, threshold table, and probability distribution over official rounded values.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Cleaner forecasts for tax parameters, benefit formulas, and other indexed statutory values.\",\"risk\":\"Overconfidence if the pack treats legal interpretation as fixed when IRS implementation could differ.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\"]},{\"priority\":\"next\",\"area\":\"ui\",\"summary\":\"Show strategy-track updates separately from final prose reasoning.\",\"rationale\":\"Prior traces and catalog priors are useful but not structured enough to compare how a new run moved the forecast.\",\"proposedChange\":\"In the UI and record schema, add a compact update table with rows for catalog prior, official latest level, model prior, inside-view adjustment, policy/formula adjustment, and final forecast. Store numeric deltas and cited evidence per row.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Reviewers can quickly see whether updates are evidence-backed or judgmental.\",\"risk\":\"May add clutter unless the UI keeps the table compact and collapsible.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"snap-max-allotment-family-4-fy2027\",\"irs-total-refunds-october-2026\",\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\"]},{\"priority\":\"later\",\"area\":\"scheduler\",\"summary\":\"Route target types to specialized prompt modes instead of sending all through the fast public-release prompt.\",\"rationale\":\"Fast mode works for many official-release forecasts but is less suitable for formula thresholds, unresolved future placeholders, and targets requiring exact vintage handling.\",\"proposedChange\":\"Add target metadata such as release_series, statutory_formula, vintage_revision, first_print_page, and survey_sampling. Use it to select public_release_fast, formula_nowcast, vintage_series, or survey_nowcast prompt modes.\",\"expectedImpact\":\"Fewer mismatched reasoning templates and more relevant evidence collection.\",\"risk\":\"Misclassification could send a simple target to an overly complex prompt.\",\"evidenceRunSlugs\":[\"ctc-maximum-per-child-ty2027\",\"medicaid-chip-enrollment-april-2026\",\"uk-unemployment-rate-jul-sep-2026\"]}],\"promptPatchCandidates\":[{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"Add a required 'Structured forecast basis' section before the final forecast: latest official level, historical sample, model prior, evidence-backed adjustments, interval method, and explicit unresolved data gaps.\"},{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"Add resolver instructions: do not use an input release date as resolutionDate when the target resolves to a later agency publication; classify the date basis and cite the official calendar, placeholder, policy deadline, or first-post fallback.\"},{\"file\":\"agents/thesis-analyst/system.md\",\"patchSummary\":\"For formula-driven targets, require a threshold table and discrete probability mass over rounded outcomes; do not force a continuous trend model when the statutory formula dominates.\"},{\"file\":\"validators/forecast-cell validation surface\",\"patchSummary\":\"Warn when reasoning says a same-series history was not fetched but the interval uses realized-volatility language; require either historicalSample values or an explicit fallback uncertainty model.\"},{\"file\":\"validators/resolution metadata validation surface\",\"patchSummary\":\"Flag resolver URLs that point to prior-year analogue pages for future first-print targets unless a stable index or future placeholder is also present.\"}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-31-57z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ga-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/draft_codex_last_message.txt:1:{\"slug\":\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ga\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"Georgia Medicaid ex parte renewal share, Aug. 2026\",\"question\":\"CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data, Georgia state row, August 2026 reporting period, original first-print submission: ex parte renewals as a share of completed Medicaid renewals.\",\"unit\":\"percent\",\"pointEstimate\":83.6,\"ciLow\":78.2,\"ciHigh\":88.9,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-12-15\",\"resolutionSource\":\"CMS, State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data (data.medicaid.gov)\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to Georgia's August 2026 reporting-period original (O) state row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c when CMS first publishes that row. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published ex parte renewal numerator divided by the published completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS print available on data.medicaid.gov and ignore later updated submissions or revisions.\",\"dataPointId\":\"cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ga.aug_2026\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"GA 2025-07 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":77.3},{\"label\":\"GA 2025-09 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":78.2},{\"label\":\"GA 2025-11 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":81.1},{\"label\":\"GA 2026-01 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":82.2},{\"label\":\"GA 2026-02 latest inspected ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":81.6}],\"drivers\":[\"Georgia's recent ex parte renewal share is already high, around the low 80s\",\"Trend from July 2025 to early 2026 is positive but flattening\",\"Renewal cohort composition can move numerator and denominator month to month\",\"Data-match coverage and eligibility-system operations govern further gains\",\"Ceiling effects limit upside relative to lower-performing states\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-28T00:33:02Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for Georgia Medicaid ex parte renewal share, August 2026\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is a Georgia state row, not a national weighted average: the original first-publication August 2026 reporting-period row in the CMS eligibility processing dataset. The target is the share of completed Medicaid renewals processed ex parte, reported in percent and rounded to one decimal.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Inspected the registered CMS Medicaid PI target and local ledger identity fields for the Georgia August 2026 ex parte renewal-share resolver.\",\"result\":\"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ga, unit percent, registered resolutionDate 2026-12-15, dataset id 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ga.aug_2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked CMS Medicaid release vehicle context preserved for this data family.\",\"result\":\"Fetched official release context that data.Medicaid.gov is updated monthly; inspected CMS page context listed Preliminary March 2026 data and June 26, 2026 as the current update date for related February 2026 and March 2026 entries.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked CMS eligibility-processing resolver fields used for this ex parte renewal-share target.\",\"result\":\"Fetched original submission status O, August 2026 reporting period, numerator as completed renewals processed through ex parte renewal, denominator as total completed renewals, and expected publication lag of about 3 to 4 months after the reporting period.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"repo.lookup\",\"call\":\"Read the local official-source-derived Georgia historical context for this exact CMS series.\",\"result\":\"Fetched Georgia values: 2025-07 = 77.3 percent, 2025-09 = 78.2 percent, 2025-11 = 81.1 percent, 2026-01 = 82.2 percent, and 2026-02 = 81.6 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"repo.lookup\",\"call\":\"Computed recent Georgia movement and latest-value anchor from the inspected sample.\",\"result\":\"Fetched latest inspected Georgia value 2026-02 = 81.6 percent; changes were +0.9 percentage points from 2025-07 to 2025-09, +2.9 from 2025-09 to 2025-11, +1.1 from 2025-11 to 2026-01, and -0.6 from 2026-01 to 2026-02.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference class: the most relevant outside view is Georgia's own recent first-print run for this CMS eligibility-processing series. The five observed points average 80.1 percent, the latest three average 81.6 percent, and the latest inspected value is 81.6 percent, so latest-value persistence with modest trend continuation is the prior.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, and mechanism: Georgia is already a high ex parte performer, so ceiling effects matter. The July-to-January improvement supports a mild upward update, but the February dip and high starting level argue against extrapolating the full 2025 trend through August.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: prior model is Georgia latest-value persistence with damped local trend, using five inspected observations from 2025-07, 2025-09, 2025-11, 2026-01, and 2026-02. Starting from latest inspected 81.6 percent, I add +1.4 pp for the 2025-to-early-2026 improvement signal and +0.6 pp for CMS compliance and continued automation drift, yielding 83.6. The 80% interval is calibrated from realized first-print movements and widened for the six-month horizon, renewal-cohort mix, and limited skipped-month sample, giving 78.2 to 88.9.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: the forecast could be too high if the 2026-01 and 2026-02 values already represent Georgia's practical ceiling or if August has a manual-heavy renewal cohort. Upside outside the interval would require a durable system or data-match improvement pushing the first print above 88.9 percent; downside outside the interval would require a data-source outage, eligibility-system issue, reporting break, or cohort mix pushing the share below 78.2 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Historical mean = (77.3 + 78.2 + 81.1 + 82.2 + 81.6) / 5 = 80.1 percent. Adjacent changes were +0.9, +2.9, +1.1, and -0.6 pp, with mean absolute change about 1.4 pp. Point calculation: 81.6 latest inspected value + 1.4 pp damped trend + 0.6 pp automation/compliance drift = 83.6 percent. Interval calculation: center 83.6, lower half-width 5.4 pp and upper half-width 5.3 pp, yielding 78.2 to 88.9 after one-decimal rounding.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resolution-date note: the canonical ledger target uses 2026-12-15, tied to CMS's monthly data.Medicaid.gov release vehicle for a three-to-four-month-lag August 2026 first print. I did not find a separate future-dated CMS placeholder in this sandbox; I keep the target's date and bind scoring to the first official CMS dataset print.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":83.6,\"ciLow\":78.2,\"ciHigh\":88.9}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-16/2026-06-16t10-08-54z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-2026-q4/stderr.txt:157:  released ~the 3rd Friday; schedule at\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-01/2026-07-01t05-12-15z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ky-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/prompt.md:20:- resolutionDate: \"2026-12-15\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-01/2026-07-01t05-12-15z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ky-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/prompt.md:106:- resolutionDate must be verified from an official release calendar or announcement schedule this run. Do not infer it from cadence.\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-01/2026-07-01t05-12-15z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ky-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/manifest.json:11:    \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-16/2026-06-16t10-08-54z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-2026-q4/prompt.md:144:  released ~the 3rd Friday; schedule at\nrecords/2026-06-15/live/spm-child-poverty-2025.json:1:{\"distribution\":{\"format\":\"numeric_cdf_v1\",\"pointCount\":201,\"support\":{\"lower\":10.25,\"upper\":16.25},\"points\":[{\"value\":10.25,\"probability\":0},{\"value\":10.28,\"probability\":0.00181818181818},{\"value\":10.31,\"probability\":0.