and CMS renewal-policy compliance pressure support persistence at a high level\",\"Manual-heavy cohorts, reporting breaks, or data-source outages are the main downside risks\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/api/1/datastore/query/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360/0\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-07-01T05:13:55Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for Kentucky Medicaid ex parte renewal share, August 2026\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is a Kentucky state row, not a national weighted average: the original first-publication August 2026 reporting-period row in CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data. The target is the share of completed Medicaid renewals processed ex parte, reported in percent and rounded to one decimal.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the CMS Medicaid.gov monthly reports page for the release vehicle and current update cadence.\",\"result\":\"Fetched official CMS monthly page evidence: Preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data was listed, and March 2026, February 2026, January 2026, December 2025, November 2025, October 2025, September 2025, August 2025, and July 2025 entries were Last Updated June 26, 2026; the page states data.Medicaid.gov is updated monthly.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the data.medicaid.gov target dataset and API identifiers for the CMS eligibility-processing series.\",\"result\":\"Fetched CMS dataset id 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c and datastore id 6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360; the target uses original submission status O, August 2026 reporting period, and a first-print resolution date of 2026-12-15 in the canonical ledger.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"repo.lookup\",\"call\":\"Read public generated official-source-derived Kentucky history for this exact CMS ex parte renewal-share series, excluding the existing catalog point and interval from evidence.\",\"result\":\"Fetched Kentucky original first-print shares: 2025-07 = 84.3 percent, 2025-09 = 88.2 percent, 2025-11 = 95.3 percent, 2026-01 = 89.6 percent, and 2026-02 = 89.9 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"shell.math\",\"call\":\"Computed summary statistics from the five inspected Kentucky official-source-derived points.\",\"result\":\"Fetched calculated summaries: five-point mean = 89.5 percent, latest-three mean = 91.6 percent, adjacent changes = +3.9, +7.1, -5.7, and +0.3 percentage points, mean absolute adjacent change = 4.3 percentage points, and observed range = 11.0 percentage points.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference-class anchor: the most relevant outside view is Kentucky's own recent original-submission first-print run for this CMS eligibility-processing series. The level is high and stable enough that latest-value persistence near 90 percent is a stronger prior than a national or multi-state average.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, and mechanism: Kentucky has already reached a high-ex-parte regime, with 2025-11 at 95.3 percent and February 2026 at 89.9 percent. Momentum is mildly positive from July 2025 to February 2026, but the January 2026 pullback shows the path is cohort-sensitive rather than a smooth trend to 100 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: prior model is Kentucky latest-value persistence blended with the latest-three mean, using the five inspected original first-print points from 2025-07, 2025-09, 2025-11, 2026-01, and 2026-02. Starting from latest 89.9 percent, I add +1.3 pp for the latest-three mean being 91.6 percent, +0.8 pp for high-level persistence and CMS compliance pressure, and 0.0 pp for the ceiling-constrained trend after the January dip, giving 92.0 after rounding. The 80% interval starts from realized first-print dispersion of 11.0 pp and mean adjacent move of 4.3 pp, widened for missing March-August first prints and skewed downward because upside is capped near 100.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: downside outside the interval would require a manual-heavy renewal cohort, data-source outage, eligibility-system issue, or reporting break pushing Kentucky below 82.8 percent. Upside outside the interval would require nearly universal ex parte processing and favorable cohort mix pushing the first print above 98.6 percent despite the natural ceiling.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Point calculation: 89.9 latest value + 1.3 pp pull toward latest-three mean of 91.6 + 0.8 pp high-level persistence/compliance adjustment = 92.0 percent after one-decimal rounding. Interval calculation: use a lower half-width of 9.2 pp and upper half-width of 6.6 pp, reflecting the 11.0 pp observed range, 4.3 pp mean absolute move, six-month missing-data horizon, and 100 percent ceiling; 92.0 - 9.2 = 82.8 and 92.0 + 6.6 = 98.6.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resolution-date note: the official CMS page verifies the monthly public data.Medicaid.gov release vehicle and current update pattern, while the canonical ledger target supplies 2026-12-15 for this August 2026 fixed-vintage row. I did not find a separate CMS future-dated placeholder for the exact Kentucky August 2026 row, so the forecast remains tied to the ledger date and resolves on the first official CMS dataset print.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":92.0,\"ciLow\":82.8,\"ciHigh\":98.6}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-01/2026-07-01t05-12-15z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ky-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/draft_codex_last_message.txt:1:{\"slug\":\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ky\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"Kentucky Medicaid ex parte ren