are\",\"value\":88.2},{\"label\":\"KY 2025-11 original first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":95.3},{\"label\":\"KY 2026-01 original first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":89.6},{\"label\":\"KY 2026-02 latest inspected original first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":89.9}],\"drivers\":[\"Kentucky's recent ex parte renewal share is already high, near 90 percent\",\"The observed series has a ceiling near 100 percent, limiting upside more than downside\",\"Renewal cohort composition can move numerator and denominator several percentage points month to month\",\"Eligibility data-match coverage and CMS renewal-policy compliance pressure support persistence at a high level\",\"Manual-heavy cohorts, reporting breaks, or data-source outages are the main downside risks\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/api/1/datastore/query/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360/0\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-07-01T05:13:55Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for Kentucky Medicaid ex parte renewal share, August 2026\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is a Kentucky state row, not a national weighted average: the original first-publication August 2026 reporting-period row in CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data. The target is the share of completed Medicaid renewals processed ex parte, reported in percent and rounded to one decimal.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the CMS Medicaid.gov monthly reports page for the release vehicle and current update cadence.\",\"result\":\"Fetched official CMS monthly page evidence: Preliminary March 2026 Applications, Eligibility, and Enrollment Data was listed, and March 2026, February 2026, January 2026, December 2025, November 2025, October 2025, September 2025, August 2025, and July 2025 entries were Last Updated June 26, 2026; the page states data.Medicaid.gov is updated monthly.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked the data.medicaid.gov target dataset and API identifiers for the CMS eligibility-processing series.\",\"result\":\"Fetched CMS dataset id 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c and datastore id 6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360; the target uses original submission status O, August 2026 reporting period, and a first-print resolution date of 2026-12-15 in the canonical ledger.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"repo.lookup\",\"call\":\"Read public generated official-source-derived Kentucky history for this exact CMS ex parte renewal-share series, excluding the existing catalog point and interval from evidence.\",\"result\":\"Fetched Kentucky original first-print shares: 2025-07 = 84.3 percent, 2025-09 = 88.2 percent, 2025-11 = 95.3 percent, 2026-01 = 89.6 percent, and 2026-02 = 89.9 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"shell.math\",\"call\":\"Computed summary statistics from the five inspected Kentucky official-source-derived points.\",\"result\":\"Fetched calculated summaries: five-point mean = 89.5 percent, latest-three mean = 91.6 percent, adjacent changes = +3.9, +7.1, -5.7, and +0.3 percentage points, mean absolute adjacent change = 4.3 percentage points, and observed range = 11.0 percentage points.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference-class anchor: the most relevant outside view is Kentucky's own recent original-submission first-print run for this CMS eligibility-processing series. The level is high and stable enough that latest-value persistence near 90 percent is a stronger prior than a national or multi-state average.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, and mechanism: Kentucky has already reached a high-ex-parte regime, with 2025-11 at 95.3 percent and February 2026 at 89.9 percent. Momentum is mildly positive from July 2025 to February 2026, but the January 2026 pullback shows the path is cohort-sensitive rather than a smooth trend to 100 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: prior model is Kentucky latest-value persistence blended with the latest-three mean, using the five inspected original first-print points from 2025-07, 2025-09, 2025-11, 2026-01, and 2026-02. Starting from latest 89.9 percent, I add +1.3 pp for the latest-three mean being 91.6 percent, +0.8 pp for high-level persistence and CMS compliance pressure, and 0.0 pp for the ceiling-constrained trend after the January dip, giving 92.0 after rounding. The 80% interval starts from realized first-print dispersion of 11.0 pp and mean adjacent move of 4.3 pp, widened for missing March-August first prints and skewed downward because upside is capped near 100.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: downside outside the interval would require a manual-heavy renewal cohort, data-source outage, eligibility-system issue, or reporting break pushing Kentucky below 82.8 percent. Upside outside the interval would require nearly universal ex parte processing and favorable cohort mix pushing the first print above 98.6 percent despite the natural ceiling.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Point calculation: 89.9 latest value + 1.3 pp pull toward latest-three mean of 91.6 + 0.8 pp high-level persistence/compliance adjustment = 92.0 percent after one-decimal rounding. Interval calculation: use a lower half-width of 9.2 pp and upper half-width of 6.6 pp, reflecting the 11.0 pp observed range, 4.3 pp mean absolute move, six-month missing-data horizon, and 100 percent ceiling; 92.0 - 9.2 = 82.8 and 92.0 + 6.6 = 98.6.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resolution-date note: the official CMS page verifies the monthly public data.Medicaid.gov release vehicle and current update pattern, while the canonical ledger target supplies 2026-12-15 for this August 2026 fixed-vintage row. I did not find a separate CMS future-dated placeholder for the exact Kentucky August 2026 row, so the forecast remains tied to the ledger date and resolves on the first official CMS dataset print.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":92.0,\"ciLow\":82.8,\"ciHigh\":98.6}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-16/2026-06-16t10-09-09z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-2026-q4/stderr.txt:160:  released ~the 3rd Friday; schedule at\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-31-57z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ga-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/pre_submit_review_prompt.md:16:- resolutionDate: \"2026-12-15\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-28/2026-06-28t00-31-57z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ga-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/pre_submit_review_prompt.md:51:{\"slug\":\"medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ga\",\"country\":\"US\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"Georgia Medicaid ex parte renewal share, Aug. 2026\",\"question\":\"CMS State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data, Georgia state row, August 2026 reporting period, original first-print submission: ex parte renewals as a share of completed Medicaid renewals.\",\"unit\":\"percent\",\"pointEstimate\":83.6,\"ciLow\":78.2,\"ciHigh\":88.9,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-12-15\",\"resolutionSource\":\"CMS, State Medicaid and CHIP Eligibility Processing Data (data.medicaid.gov)\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to Georgia's August 2026 reporting-period original (O) state row in CMS dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c when CMS first publishes that row. Compute ex parte renewal share as the published ex parte renewal numerator divided by the published completed-renewal denominator, multiplied by 100 and rounded to one decimal percent. Use the first official CMS print available on data.medicaid.gov and ignore later updated submissions or revisions.\",\"dataPointId\":\"cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ga.aug_2026\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"GA 2025-07 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":77.3},{\"label\":\"GA 2025-09 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":78.2},{\"label\":\"GA 2025-11 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":81.1},{\"label\":\"GA 2026-01 first-print ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":82.2},{\"label\":\"GA 2026-02 latest inspected ex parte renewal share\",\"value\":81.6}],\"drivers\":[\"Georgia's recent ex parte renewal share is already high, around the low 80s\",\"Trend from July 2025 to early 2026 is positive but flattening\",\"Renewal cohort composition can move numerator and denominator month to month\",\"Data-match coverage and eligibility-system operations govern further gains\",\"Ceiling effects limit upside relative to lower-performing states\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data/monthly-medicaid-chip-application-eligibility-determination-and-enrollment-reports-data\",\"https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid/national-medicaid-chip-program-information/medicaid-chip-enrollment-data\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c\",\"https://data.medicaid.gov/dataset/6165f45b-ca93-5bb5-9d06-db29c692a360\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-28T00:33:02Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for Georgia Medicaid ex parte renewal share, August 2026\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is a Georgia state row, not a national weighted average: the original first-publication August 2026 reporting-period row in the CMS eligibility processing dataset. The target is the share of completed Medicaid renewals processed ex parte, reported in percent and rounded to one decimal.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Inspected the registered CMS Medicaid PI target and local ledger identity fields for the Georgia August 2026 ex parte renewal-share resolver.\",\"result\":\"Fetched canonical slug medicaid-ex-parte-share-aug-2026-ga, unit percent, registered resolutionDate 2026-12-15, dataset id 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c, and dataPointId cms.medicaid_pi.ex_parte_renewal_share.ga.aug_2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked CMS Medicaid release vehicle context preserved for this data family.\",\"result\":\"Fetched official release context that data.Medicaid.gov is updated monthly; inspected CMS page context listed Preliminary March 2026 data and June 26, 2026 as the current update date for related February 2026 and March 2026 entries.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Checked CMS eligibility-processing resolver fields used for this ex parte renewal-share target.\",\"result\":\"Fetched original submission status O, August 2026 reporting period, numerator as completed renewals processed through ex parte renewal, denominator as total completed renewals, and expected publication lag of about 3 to 4 months after the reporting period.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"repo.lookup\",\"call\":\"Read the local official-source-derived Georgia historical context for this exact CMS series.\",\"result\":\"Fetched Georgia values: 2025-07 = 77.3 percent, 2025-09 = 78.2 percent, 2025-11 = 81.1 percent, 2026-01 = 82.2 percent, and 2026-02 = 81.6 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"repo.lookup\",\"call\":\"Computed recent Georgia movement and latest-value anchor from the inspected sample.\",\"result\":\"Fetched latest inspected Georgia value 2026-02 = 81.6 percent; changes were +0.9 percentage points from 2025-07 to 2025-09, +2.9 from 2025-09 to 2025-11, +1.1 from 2025-11 to 2026-01, and -0.6 from 2026-01 to 2026-02.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference class: the most relevant outside view is Georgia's own recent first-print run for this CMS eligibility-processing series. The five observed points average 80.1 percent, the latest three average 81.6 percent, and the latest inspected value is 81.6 percent, so latest-value persistence with modest trend continuation is the prior.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Level, momentum, and mechanism: Georgia is already a high ex parte performer, so ceiling effects matter. The July-to-January improvement supports a mild upward update, but the February dip and high starting level argue against extrapolating the full 2025 trend through August.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Prior/update/interval: prior model is Georgia latest-value persistence with damped local trend, using five inspected observations from 2025-07, 2025-09, 2025-11, 2026-01, and 2026-02. Starting from latest inspected 81.6 percent, I add +1.4 pp for the 2025-to-early-2026 improvement signal and +0.6 pp for CMS compliance and continued automation drift, yielding 83.6. The 80% interval is calibrated from realized first-print movements and widened for the six-month horizon, renewal-cohort mix, and limited skipped-month sample, giving 78.2 to 88.9.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: the forecast could be too high if the 2026-01 and 2026-02 values already represent Georgia's practical ceiling or if August has a manual-heavy renewal cohort. Upside outside the interval would require a durable system or data-match improvement pushing the first print above 88.9 percent; downside outside the interval would require a data-source outage, eligibility-system issue, reporting break, or cohort mix pushing the share below 78.2 percent.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Historical mean = (77.3 + 78.2 + 81.1 + 82.2 + 81.6) / 5 = 80.1 percent. Adjacent changes were +0.9, +2.9, +1.1, and -0.6 pp, with mean absolute change about 1.4 pp. Point calculation: 81.6 latest inspected value + 1.4 pp damped trend + 0.6 pp automation/compliance drift = 83.6 percent. Interval calculation: center 83.6, lower half-width 5.4 pp and upper half-width 5.3 pp, yielding 78.2 to 88.9 after one-decimal rounding.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Resolution-date note: the canonical ledger target uses 2026-12-15, tied to CMS's monthly data.Medicaid.gov release vehicle for a three-to-four-month-lag August 2026 first print. I did not find a separate future-dated CMS placeholder in this sandbox; I keep the target's date and bind scoring to the first official CMS dataset print.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":83.6,\"ciLow\":78.2,\"ciHigh\":88.9}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-16/2026-06-16t12-28-25z-boe-bank-rate-2026-06-18/raw_response.txt:1:{\"slug\":\"boe-bank-rate-2026-06-18\",\"country\":\"UK\",\"type\":\"data\",\"title\":\"BoE Bank Rate, 18 Jun 2026\",\"question\":\"Bank of England Bank Rate after the 18 June 2026 MPC announcement, percent, first official print.\",\"unit\":\"percent\",\"pointEstimate\":3.75,\"ciLow\":3.5,\"ciHigh\":4,\"confidence\":0.8,\"resolutionDate\":\"2026-06-18\",\"resolutionSource\":\"Bank of England Monetary Policy Summary and minutes of the Monetary Policy Committee meeting - June 2026\",\"resolutionSourceUrl\":\"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy-summary-and-minutes/2026/june-2026\",\"resolutionRule\":\"Resolve to the Bank Rate percentage stated in the first Bank of England June 2026 MPC Monetary Policy Summary page published on 18 June 2026, expected at 12pm UK time. Use the stated policy rate in percent; ignore later revisions, commentary, or subsequent MPC decisions unless the first page is corrected before any public value is visible.\",\"dataPointId\":\"boe.mpc.bank_rate.2026-06-18.first_print\",\"historicalContext\":[{\"label\":\"latest current Bank Rate on BoE interest-rate page\",\"value\":3.75},{\"label\":\"April 2026 MPC Bank Rate\",\"value\":3.75},{\"label\":\"March 2026 MPC Bank Rate\",\"value\":3.75},{\"label\":\"February 2026 MPC Bank Rate\",\"value\":3.75},{\"label\":\"current inflation rate on BoE interest-rate page\",\"value\":2.8},{\"label\":\"CPI inflation cited in April MPC summary\",\"value\":3.3}],\"drivers\":[\"current Bank Rate is already 3.75%\",\"June MPC announcement is scheduled for 18 June 2026\",\"April vote was 8-1 to hold, with one 4.00% dissent\",\"March vote was unanimous to hold at 3.75%\",\"February vote was 5-4 to hold, with four 3.50% cut dissents\",\"BoE says inflation and energy shocks raise upside risk\",\"loosening labour market and weak activity argue against a hike\"],\"sourceContext\":[\"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/\",\"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy/the-interest-rate-bank-rate\",\"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy/upcoming-mpc-dates\",\"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy-summary-and-minutes/2026/june-2026\",\"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy-summary-and-minutes/2026/april-2026\",\"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy-summary-and-minutes/2026/march-2026\",\"https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy-summary-and-minutes/2026/february-2026\"],\"runAt\":\"2026-06-16T12:28:37Z\",\"reasoning\":[{\"kind\":\"heading\",\"text\":\"Forecast for the 18 June 2026 Bank of England Bank Rate decision\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The resolver is the first official Bank of England June 2026 MPC Monetary Policy Summary page. Because Bank Rate is a policy decision level, the target is the rate after the announcement, not a later revised statistical series.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the Bank of England home page and current Bank Rate module.\",\"result\":\"Fetched Current Bank Rate 3.75%, Next due 18 June 2026, and current inflation rate 2.8%.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the Bank of England interest rates and Bank Rate page.\",\"result\":\"Fetched Current Bank Rate 3.75%, latest decision held at 3.75%, published 30 April 2026, inflation 3.3%, and next due 18 June 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the Bank of England MPC dates page for 2026 and 2027.\",\"result\":\"Fetched confirmed 2026 MPC dates including Thursday 5 February, 19 March, 30 April, 18 June, 30 July, 17 September, 5 November, 17 December; current Bank Rate 3.75%; next due 18 June 2026.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened the June 2026 MPC page placeholder.\",\"result\":\"Fetched page title for June 2026 MPC Summary, Published on 18 June 2026, and statement that it will be published on 18 June 2026 at 12pm.\"},{\"kind\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"official.lookup\",\"call\":\"Opened recent official MPC summaries for February, March, and April 2026.\",\"result\":\"Fetched February Bank Rate 3.75% with 5-4 vote and four preferring 3.5%; March Bank Rate 3.75% with unanimous hold; April Bank Rate 3.75% with 8-1 vote and one preferring 4.0%.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Base-rate/reference-class step: the last three MPC meetings all held at 3.75%, and the most recent vote distribution shifted from February cut dissents to March unanimous hold to April one hike dissent, so the modal reference case for the next meeting is another hold at 3.75%.\"},{\"kind\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Counter-consideration: upside inflation and energy-price risks make a 4.00% hike plausible, while weak activity and a loosening labour market keep a 3.50% cut in the broader 80% set; both alternatives are less likely than a hold two days before the scheduled release.\"},{\"kind\":\"math\",\"text\":\"Use the BoE's usual 0.25 percentage-point policy grid. Point estimate is the modal hold, 3.75. For an 80% interval, include the adjacent cut and hike outcomes around the modal decision: ciLow = 3.50, point = 3.75, ciHigh = 4.00.\"},{\"kind\":\"forecast\",\"point\":3.75,\"ciLow\":3.5,\"ciHigh\":4}]}\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-07-01/2026-07-01t05-10-12z-cms-medicaid-pi-ex-parte-renewal-share-ks-aug-2026-august-2026-reporting-period/normalized_cells.json:13:  \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\",\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-