026-q4/stderr.txt:1225:./records/2026-06-13/digest.json:3113:   \"resolutionDate\": \"2026-12-15\"\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-16/2026-06-16t10-20-32z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-2026-q4/stderr.txt:1226:./records/2026-06-\\\"text\\\":\\\"Forecast BEA Medicare government social benefits for May 2026\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The resolver is the first BEA Personal Income and Outlays release value for May 2026 Medicare government social benefits in NIPA Table 2.6, reported as seasonally adjusted annual-rate billions of dollars.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked BEA release schedule for Personal Income and Outlays, May 2026.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"BEA schedule lists Personal Income and Outlays, May 2026 on June 25, 2026 at 8:30 AM; the schedule page also showed June 24, June 25, July 7, and July 30 release dates around it.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked BEA April 2026 Personal Income and Outlays release for next-release confirmation and Table 2.6 linkage.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"BEA April 2026 release was issued May 28, 2026; it says next release is June 25, 2026 at 8:30 a.m. EDT for Personal Income and Outlays, May 2026, and links Table 2.6.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"history.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked FRED mirror of BEA series W824RC1 for recent monthly history and metadata.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"FRED/BEA W824RC1 shows Apr 2026 1321.7, Mar 2026 1311.4, Feb 2026 1301.0, Jan 2026 1290.6, Dec 2025 1280.1; units are billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted annual rate, monthly, updated May 28, 2026.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Reference-class/base-rate: this administered-benefit line has recently moved in very smooth monthly steps. The last four month-to-month changes are +10.5, +10.4, +10.4, and +10.3 billion, so a one-month extrapolation is a strong baseline.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Using the recent monthly increments, average change from Dec 2025 to Apr 2026 is (1321.7 - 1280.1) / 4 = 10.4. Point forecast = 1321.7 + 10.3 rounded to one decimal = 1332.0. I use an 80% interval of +/-6.0 around the point to allow first-print source-data noise and possible BEA monthly allocation changes.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-consideration: the run-up could deviate if BEA incorporates updated Medicare administrative source data or seasonal factors in the May first print; however, the recent level path and annual-rate reporting make a sharp break less likely than another near-10-billion step.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":1332.0,\\\"ciLow\\\":1326.0,\\\"ciHigh\\\":1338.0}]}\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-17-15z-bls-jolts-job-openings-2026-05/parsed_cells.json:32:        \\\"label\\\": \\\"Jan 2026\\\",\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-17-15z-bls-jolts-job-openings-2026-05/parsed_cells.json:78:        \\\"result\\\": \\\"FRED/BLS series JTSJOL lists Apr 2026 7,618, Mar 2026 6,887, Feb 2026 6,922, Jan 2026 7,240, Dec 2025 6,550, all in thousands.\\\"\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-10-16z-eurostat-hicp-flash-yoy-2026-06/stdout.txt:1:{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"eurostat-hicp-flash-yoy-2026-06\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"EA\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"data\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Euro area HICP flash inflation, June 2026\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Eurostat euro area all-items HICP annual inflation flash estimate for June 2026, year-on-year percent change, first print\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"percent\\\",\\\"pointEstimate\\\":3.3,\\\"ciLow\\\":2.8,\\\"ciHigh\\\":3.9,\\\"confidence\\\":0.8,\\\"resolutionDate\\\":\\\"2026-07-01\\\",\\\"resolutionSource\\\":\\\"Eurostat Euro indicators flash estimate release for euro area annual inflation\\\",\\\"resolutionSourceUrl\\\":\\\"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-euro-indicators\\\",\\\"resolutionRule\\\":\\\"Resolve to the first Eurostat flash-estimate print of euro area all-items HICP annual inflation for June 2026, reported to one decimal percent. Use the value first published in the Euro indicators release; ignore later complete HICP releases or revisions.\\\",\\\"dataPointId\\\":\\\"eurostat.prc_hicp_minr.ea.all_items.2026-06.first_print\\\",\\\"historicalContext\\\":[{\\\"label\\\":\\\"2026-01 flash/all-items annual rate\\\",\\\"value\\\":1.7},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"2026-02 flash/all-items annual rate\\\",\\\"value\\\":1.9},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"2026-03 flash/all-items annual rate\\\",\\\"value\\\":2.6},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"2026-04 flash/all-items annual rate\\\",\\\"value\\\":3.0},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"latest 2026-05 flash/all-items annual rate\\\",\\\"value\\\":3.2}],\\\"drivers\\\":[\\\"May flash inflation already at 3.2 percent\\\",\\\"energy contribution still elevated at 10.9 percent year over year\\\",\\\"services inflation rose to 3.5 percent in May\\\",\\\"recent monthly headline momentum positive but May monthly rate only 0.1 percent\\\",\\\"one-decimal Eurostat flash print limits useful precision\\\"],\\\"sourceContext\\\":[\\\"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-euro-indicators/w/2-02062026-ap\\\",\\\"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/hicp\\\",\\\"https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/main/news/euro-indicators/release-calendar\\\"],\\\"runAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-17T02:10:25Z\\\",\\\"reasoning\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"heading\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Euro area HICP flash inflation forecast for June 2026\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The resolver is the first Eurostat Euro indicators flash-estimate release for euro area all-items HICP annual inflation for June 2026, not the later complete HICP data release or any revision.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Eurostat HICP overview page for the current inflation news item and data context.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Eurostat HICP overview listed latest news on 2 June 2026 as euro area annual inflation up to 3.2% and also listed 20 May 2026 annual inflation up to 3.0%.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened Eurostat Euro indicators flash estimate for May 2026.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched headline all-items HICP annual rates: Jan 2026 1.7, Feb 2026 1.9, Mar 2026 2.6, Apr 2026 3.0, May 2026 3.2e; May monthly rate 0.1e.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Read the May 2026 Eurostat flash-estimate component table.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched May 2026 component annual rates: energy 10.9%, services 3.5%, food alcohol and tobacco 2.0%, non-energy industrial goods 0.9%; April comparators were energy 10.8%, services 3.0%, food alcohol and tobacco 2.4%, goods 0.8%.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked Eurostat release scheduling information on the May 2026 flash release and the Euro indicators calendar page.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"The May 2026 flash release says Next release: 1 July 2026; the release-calendar page identifies Inflation as a Euro indicator and states the calendar uses Europe/Luxembourg time zone.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base rate/reference class: the last four month-to-month changes in the first-print annual rate were +0.2, +0.7, +0.4, and +0.2 percentage points, but monthly headline inflation in May was only 0.1 percent, so a naive continuation of the rapid March-May rise should be tempered.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Starting from May's 3.2%, I add 0.1 percentage point for continued energy and services pressure but shrink the recent +0.375 average change toward zero because the May monthly rate was only 0.1%; rounded to Eurostat's one-decimal convention this gives 3.3%. An 80% interval of roughly +/-0.55 percentage point around 3.3 rounds to 2.8% to 3.9%.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-consideration: energy inflation was already very high at 10.9% and could mean-revert or face less favorable base effects in June, while food inflation eased to 2.0%; those factors keep the lower side materially plausible despite the high latest headline.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":3.3,\\\"ciLow\\\":2.8,\\\"ciHigh\\\":3.9}]}\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-21-59z-bls-cpi-u-headline-mom-2026-06/cells.with_activity.json:77:        \\\"result\\\": \\\"All items m/m SA: Dec 2025 0.3, Jan 2026 0.2, Feb 2026 0.3, Mar 2026 0.9, Apr 2026 0.6, May 2026 0.5.\\\"\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-17-15z-bls-jolts-job-openings-2026-05/stdout.txt:1:{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"bls-jolts-job-openings-2026-05\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"US\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"data\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"US JOLTS job openings, May 2026\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"What will the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics first report for seasonally adjusted total nonfarm job openings in the Job Openings and Labor Turnover Survey for May 2026?\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"thousands\\\",\\\"pointEstimate\\\":7450,\\\"ciLow\\\":6850,\\\"ciHigh\\\":8050,\\\"confidence\\\":0.8,\\\"resolutionDate\\\":\\\"2026-06-30\\\",\\\"resolutionSource\\\":\\\"Official agency release\\\",\\\"resolutionSourceUrl\\\":\\\"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/jolts.nr0.htm\\\",\\\"resolutionRule\\\":\\\"Resolve to the first BLS Job Openings and Labor Turnover Survey news-release print for May 2026, seasonally adjusted total nonfarm job openings, expressed in thousands. Use the value published in the initial June 30, 2026 release and ignore later revisions or benchmark updates.\\\",\\\"dataPointId\\\":\\\"bls.jolts.job_openings.2026-05.first_print\\\",\\\"historicalContext\\\":[{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Apr 2026\\\",\\\"value\\\":7618},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Mar 2026\\\",\\\"value\\\":6887},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Feb 2026\\\",\\\"value\\\":6922},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Jan 2026\\\",\\\"value\\\":7240},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Dec 2025\\\",\\\"value\\\":6550}],\\\"drivers\\\":[\\\"April openings jumped sharply but look partly concentrated and noisy\\\",\\\"May payroll growth was solid at 172,000 and unemployment held at 4.3 percent\\\",\\\"Hires weakened to 5,116 thousand in April, arguing against a sustained openings surge\\\",\\\"Recent JOLTS levels cluster around 6.9 to 7.6 million\\\"],\\\"sourceContext\\\":[\\\"https://www.bls.gov/schedule/news_release/jolts.htm\\\",\\\"https://www.bls.gov/jlt/\\\",\\\"https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/JTSJOL\\\",\\\"https://www.bls.gov/news.release/empsit.nr0.htm\\\"],\\\"runAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-17T02:17:25Z\\\",\\\"reasoning\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"heading\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Forecast for May 2026 BLS JOLTS job openings\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The target is the first official BLS JOLTS print for seasonally adjusted total nonfarm job openings in May 2026, reported in thousands; later revisions do not count.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked the BLS JOLTS release calendar for the May 2026 reference month.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"BLS lists May 2026 JOLTS for release on Jun. 30, 2026 at 10:00 AM.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked the BLS JOLTS program page latest levels table.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"BLS latest levels show Apr 2026 job openings 7,618 thousand, hires 5,116 thousand, total separations 4,978 thousand, job openings rate 4.6 percent, hires rate 3.2 percent, quits rate 1.9 percent, layoffs/discharges rate 1.1 percent.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"history.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked the FRED mirror of BLS series JTSJOL for recent total nonfarm job openings history.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"FRED/BLS series JTSJOL lists Apr 2026 7,618, Mar 2026 6,887, Feb 2026 6,922, Jan 2026 7,240, Dec 2025 6,550, all in thousands.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked the BLS May 2026 Employment Situation release for near-contemporaneous labor-market context.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"BLS reported May 2026 payroll employment +172,000, unemployment rate 4.3 percent, April payroll revision to +179,000, and March payroll revision to +214,000.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base-rate/reference class: month-to-month JOLTS job openings are noisy and often revise, so I anchor on the recent five-month range of 6,550 to 7,618 thousand and the latest three-month average near 7,142 thousand rather than extrapolating the full April jump.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The upside case is that solid May payroll growth and stable unemployment mean labor demand remained firm, so April's 7,618 thousand could persist into May.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-consideration: April's 731 thousand openings increase was unusually large while hires fell to 5,116 thousand, so some mean reversion or measurement noise is plausible in the first May print.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Anchor around Apr 2026 7,618 and recent three-month average (7,618 + 6,887 + 6,922) / 3 = 7,142; weighting April persistence against mean reversion gives about 7,450 thousand. An 80 percent interval of 6,850 to 8,050 allows roughly +/-600 thousand, covering typical JOLTS volatility and the April spike risk.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":7450,\\\"ciLow\\\":6850,\\\"ciHigh\\\":8050}]}\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-17-15z-bls-jolts-job-openings-2026-05/cells.with_activity.json:32:        \\\"label\\\": \\\"Jan 2026\\\",\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/2026-06-17t02-17-15z-bls-jolts-job-openings-2026-05/cells.with_activity.json:78:        \\\"result\\\": \\\"FRED/BLS series JTSJOL lists Apr 2026 7,618, Mar 2026 6,887, Feb 2026 6,922, Jan 2026 7,240, Dec 2025 6,550, all in thousands.\\\"\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-17/