ext release date Jul 2, 2026.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base-rate/reference class: one-month moves in the rounded unemployment rate are usually small, and the immediate recent reference class is especially persistent: five latest monthly values are all between 4.3 and 4.4, with four of five at 4.3.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The main upside risk is that the household survey can be noisy and BLS says the unemployment-rate monthly-change confidence interval is about plus or minus 0.3 percentage point near a 6.0 percent rate; a softer June household survey could round to 4.4 or 4.5 even if payrolls remain positive.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The main downside risk is continued strong labor demand: May payrolls rose 172,000, participation was steady at 61.8 percent, and the unemployment rate has held at 4.3 despite month-to-month changes in unemployment levels.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Use persistence as the anchor: median of Jan-May rounded rates = 4.3. Apply no drift because May payrolls were strong and participation was flat, but widen the 80 percent interval to roughly one BLS household-survey rounded-rate move below and above: 4.1 to 4.6.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":4.3,\\\"ciLow\\\":4.1,\\\"ciHigh\\\":4.6}]}\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-29-23z-usda-fns-wic-total-participants-march-2026-fixed-vintage-march-2026-fixed-vintage/revision_prompt.md:112:{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"usda-fns-wic-total-participants-march-2026-fixed-vintage\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"US\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"data\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"US WIC participants, Mar 2026\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"USDA Food and Nutrition Service WIC total participants for March 2026, national monthly data, first preliminary print/fixed vintage, not revised values\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"count\\\",\\\"pointEstimate\\\":6701661,\\\"ciLow\\\":6701660,\\\"ciHigh\\\":6701662,\\\"confidence\\\":0.8,\\\"resolutionDate\\\":\\\"2026-06-12\\\",\\\"resolutionSource\\\":\\\"USDA Food and Nutrition Service WIC Participation and Costs monthly data, FY 2026 preliminary fixed vintage\\\",\\\"resolutionSourceUrl\\\":\\\"https://fns-prod.azureedge.us/sites/default/files/resource-files/37wic-monthly-6.pdf\\\",\\\"resolutionRule\\\":\\\"Resolve to the first USDA FNS WIC Participation and Costs monthly-data print that includes March 2026 total participants, using the published whole-participant count in the Total Participants column. Do not use later revised vintages, FRED, or mirrors; revisions after the first March 2026 print are ignored.\\\",\\\"dataPointId\\\":\\\"usda.fns.wic.total_participants.2026-03.first_print\\\",\\\"historicalContext\\\":[{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Mar 2026 first print\\\",\\\"value\\\":6701661},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Feb 2026 prior-month print in same vintage\\\",\\\"value\\\":6664580},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Mar 2025 same-month revised comparison\\\",\\\"value\\\":6850836},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Jan 2026 same-vintage recent point\\\",\\\"value\\\":6696300},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Nov 2025 earlier vintage first print\\\",\\\"value\\\":6752138}],\\\"drivers\\\":[\\\"March normally rebounds from February in WIC participation\\\",\\\"FY 2026 participation was running below FY 2025 after a sharp November 2025 drop\\\",\\\"Same-vintage February 2026 to March 2026 increase was visible in the official first print\\\",\\\"Official FNS source had already posted the March 2026 fixed vintage at run time\\\",\\\"Residual uncertainty is limited to transcription or selecting the wrong vintage, not economic forecasting error\\\"],\\\"sourceContext\\\":[\\\"https://www.fns.usda.gov/pd/wic-program\\\",\\\"https://fns-prod.azureedge.us/sites/default/files/resource-files/37wic-monthly-6.pdf\\\",\\\"https://fns-prod.azureedge.us/sites/default/files/resource-files/37wic-monthly-5.pdf\\\"],\\\"runAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-27T13:29:28Z\\\",\\\"reasoning\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"heading\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"USDA FNS WIC total participants, March 2026 fixed vintage\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The resolver is the USDA Food and Nutrition Service WIC Participation and Costs monthly table, national Total Participants, March 2026, first preliminary print. Because the official fixed-vintage PDF already included March 2026 at run time, this is treated as a post-release fixed-vintage cell with only transcription and vintage-selection uncertainty.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened the USDA FNS WIC Data Tables page to identify the official source family and available resource links.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"The official WIC Data Tables page listed FY 2026 preliminary monthly state-level data and Monthly Data - National Level, with page updated 2026-02-24 and links to official FNS resource files.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened the official FNS March-inclusive national monthly PDF at 37wic-monthly-6.pdf.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"The PDF states Data as of June 12, 2026; March 2026 values are Women 1,458,253, Infant 1,419,036, Children 3,824,372, Total Participants 6,701,661, Food Costs 431,316,601, NSA Costs 165,990,106, Average Food Cost 64.36.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Fetched same-vintage nearby official observations from the March-inclusive PDF.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Same-vintage FY 2026 recent totals were Nov 2025 6,771,734, Dec 2025 6,712,611, Jan 2026 6,696,300, Feb 2026 6,664,580, and Mar 2026 6,701,661.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Fetched the immediately prior official vintage to check the vintage boundary and revision behavior.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"The prior 37wic-monthly-5.pdf states Data as of May 8, 2026 and included Feb 2026 Total Participants 6,640,819 but did not include Mar 2026; therefore the June 12, 2026 PDF is the first fetched official print containing Mar 2026.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Fetched the recent official-source reference class from the March-inclusive PDF and older official monthly rows.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Recent same-month and nearby totals were Mar 2025 6,850,836, Feb 2025 6,802,175, Apr 2025 6,877,215, Mar 2024 6,680,974, and Mar 2023 6,621,311.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base-rate/reference-class view: March participation often sits above February, with Mar 2025 exceeding Feb 2025 by 48,661 and Mar 2024 exceeding Feb 2024 by 35,336. The same-vintage FY 2026 pattern is consistent with that seasonal rebound, from 6,664,580 in February to 6,701,661 in March.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-consideration: if this needed an ex-ante forecast before the June 12 official vintage, the late-2025 downshift and February weakness would have argued for a wider interval around roughly the high-6.6-million to low-6.7-million range. Once the first official print is fetched, that uncertainty is dominated by avoiding later revisions and matching the printed whole-count precision.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Point uses the official first-print total directly: 1,458,253 women + 1,419,036 infants + 3,824,372 children = 6,701,661 total participants. The 80% interval is set to 6,701,660 to 6,701,662, one participant around the printed whole-count total, to reflect only transcription/vintage-selection risk after the official fixed vintage is observed.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":6701661,\\\"ciLow\\\":6701660,\\\"ciHigh\\\":6701662}]}\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-34-28z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-april-to-june-2026-first-print-apr-jun-2026/raw_response.txt:1:{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"uk-ons-unemployment-rate-apr-jun-2026-first-print\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"UK\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"data\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"UK unemployment Apr-Jun 2026\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"ONS UK unemployment rate for people aged 16 years and over, seasonally adjusted Labour Force Survey estimate, April to June 2026, first print\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"percent\\\",\\\"pointEstimate\\\":5.1,\\\"ciLow\\\":4.7,\\\"ciHigh\\\":5.5,\\\"confidence\\\":0.8,\\\"resolutionDate\\\":\\\"2026-08-11\\\",\\\"resolutionSource\\\":\\\"Office for National Statistics Labour market overview, UK: August 2026\\\",\\\"resolutionSourceUrl\\\":\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/releases/labourmarketoverviewukaugust2026\\\",\\\"resolutionRule\\\":\\\"Resolve to the first ONS-published UK unemployment rate for people aged 16 years and over for April to June 2026, seasonally adjusted, in the August 2026 Labour market overview or linked ONS time-series page. Use the one-decimal percent first print only; ignore later revisions or reweighting changes published after the first print.\\\",\\\"dataPointId\\\":\\\"ons.lms.unemployment_rate_16plus.apr_jun_2026.first_print\\\",\\\"historicalContext\\\":[{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Nov 2025-Jan 2026 unemployment rate, percent\\\",\\\"value\\\":5.2},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Dec 2025-Feb 2026 unemployment rate, percent\\\",\\\"value\\\":4.9},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Jan-Mar 2026 unemployment rate, percent\\\",\\\"value\\\":5.0},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Feb-Apr 2026 unemployment rate, percent\\\",\\\"value\\\":4.9},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Mar-May 2026 vacancies, thousands\\\",\\\"value\\\":707},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"May 2026 claimant count, millions\\\",\\\"value\\\":1.712}],\\\"drivers\\\":[\\\"recent LFS unemployment has held near 5 percent\\\",\\\"vacancies are at a five-year low\\\",\\\"PAYE payroll has weakened into spring\\\",\\\"claimant count is rising\\\",\\\"LFS volatility argues for a wider interval\\\"],\\\"sourceContext\\\":[\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/bulletins/uklabourmarket/june2026\\\",\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/bulletins/uklabourmarket/may2026\\\",\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/bulletins/uklabourmarket/april2026\\\",\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/employmentandlabourmarket/peopleinwork/employmentandemployeetypes/bulletins/uklabourmarket/march2026\\\",\\\"https://www.ons.gov.uk/releases/labourmarketoverviewukaugust2026\\\"],\\\"runAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-27T13:39:06Z\\\",\\\"reasoning\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"heading\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Forecast UK Apr-Jun 2026 unemployment first print\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The resolver is the first ONS print of the seasonally adjusted UK unemployment rate for people aged 16 years and over covering April to June 2026. ONS labour-market rates are reported to one decimal percent, and later revisions should not change the resolved value.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened ONS Labour market overview, UK: June 2026 for the latest LFS and labour-market indicators.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched February to April 2026 unemployment rate 4.9%, employment rate 75.0%, economic inactivity rate 21.0%, May 2026 claimant count 1.712 million, vacancies 707,000, payrolled employees down 31,000 over the comparable quarter and May payroll up 2,000 on the month.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened ONS Labour market overview, UK: May 2026 for the prior first-print LFS reference point.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched January to March 2026 unemployment rate 5.0%, employment rate 75.0%, economic inactivity rate 20.9%, April 2026 claimant count 1.699 million, vacancies 705,000, and April payrolled employees down 100,000 on the month.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened ONS Labour market overview, UK: April 2026 and March 2026 for the recent reference class.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched December 2025 to February 2026 unemployment rate 4.9%, January to March 2026 vacancies 711,000, November 2025 to January 2026 unemployment rate 5.2%, and December 2025 to February 2026 vacancies 721,000.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Checked the official ONS release placeholder for Labour market overview, UK: August 2026.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Fetched scheduled August 2026 labour-market first-print release date 11 August 2026 for the Apr-Jun 2026 three-month LFS unemployment estimate.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base-rate/reference-class anchor: the model prior is a persistence/recent-mean time-series prior rather than a separate fitted model, because only a short official first-print window is being used in this fast run. The last four available rolling three-month first prints are 5.2, 4.9, 5.0, and 4.9, averaging 5.0.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Level and momentum: unemployment is already near 5%, vacancies have moved from 721,000 to 711,000 to 705,000 to 707,000, and claimant count rose to 1.712 million. These indicators point to a small upward adjustment in the Apr-Jun LFS unemployment target, not a large break.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-consideration: LFS estimates remain volatile and ONS warns against over-reading short-term movements; May payroll was nearly flat after the April drop, so a continuation at 4.9 or a dip to 4.8 remains plausible if survey composition offsets payroll weakness.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Start with recent first-print mean (5.2+4.9+5.0+4.9)/4 = 5.0. Add 0.1 percentage point for weak vacancies, rising claimant count, and spring PAYE weakness, giving 5.1. Use an 80% interval of 4.7 to 5.5: roughly the 5.1 center plus or minus 0.4, widened for LFS volatility and possible seasonal-adjustment/reweighting noise.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Upside scenario: April-June layoffs and hiring freezes show through clearly in the LFS and unemployment prints 5.4 or 5.5. Downside scenario: April payroll weakness is revised away and survey volatility holds unemployment near 4.8 or 4.9. Outside-the-interval scenarios require either a sharp labour-market break above 5.5 or a strong participation/employment surprise below 4.7.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Review disposition: accepted the resolver critique by making the August 2026 ONS release placeholder the explicit date source, accepted the model-prior critique by naming the persistence/recent-mean prior, and accepted the optional unit-label clarification for historical context.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":5.1,\\\"ciLow\\\":4.7,\\\"ciHigh\\\":5.5}]}\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-29-23z-usda-fns-wic-total-participants-march-2026-fixed-vintage-march-2026-fixed-vintage/draft_codex_last_message.txt:1:{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"usda-fns-wic-total-participants-march-2026-fixed-vintage\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"US\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"data\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"US WIC participants, Mar 2026\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"USDA Food and Nutrition Service WIC total participants for March 2026, national monthly data, first preliminary print/fixed vintage, not revised values\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"count\\\",\\\"pointEstimate\\\":6701661,\\\"ciLow\\\":6701660,\\\"ciHigh\\\":6701662,\\\"confidence\\\":0.8,\\\"resolutionDate\\\":\\\"2026-06-12\\\",\\\"resolutionSource\\\":\\\"USDA Food and Nutrition Service WIC Participation and Costs monthly data, FY 2026 preliminary fixed vintage\\\",\\\"resolutionSourceUrl\\\":\\\"https://fns-prod.azureedge.us/sites/default/files/resource-files/37wic-monthly-6.pdf\\\",\\\"resolutionRule\\\":\\\"Resolve to the first USDA FNS WIC Participation and Costs monthly-data print that includes March 2026 total participants, using the published whole-participant count in the Total Participants column. Do not use later revised vintages, FRED, or mirrors; revisions after the first March 2026 print are ignored.\\\",\\\"dataPointId\\\":\\\"usda.fns.wic.total_participants.2026-03.first_print\\\",\\\"historicalContext\\\":[{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Mar 2026 first print\\\",\\\"value\\\":6701661},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Feb 2026 prior-month print in same vintage\\\",\\\"value\\\":6664580},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Mar 2025 same-month revised comparison\\\",\\\"value\\\":6850836},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Jan 2026 same-vintage recent point\\\",\\\"value\\\":6696300},{\\\"label\\\":\\\"Nov 2025 earlier vintage first print\\\",\\\"value\\\":6752138}],\\\"drivers\\\":[\\\"March normally rebounds from February in WIC participation\\\",\\\"FY 2026 participation was running below FY 2025 after a sharp November 2025 drop\\\",\\\"Same-vintage February 2026 to March 2026 increase was visible in the official first print\\\",\\\"Official FNS source had already posted the March 2026 fixed vintage at run time\\\",\\\"Residual uncertainty is limited to transcription or selecting the wrong vintage, not economic forecasting error\\\"],\\\"sourceContext\\\":[\\\"https://www.fns.usda.gov/pd/wic-program\\\",\\\"https://fns-prod.azureedge.us/sites/default/files/resource-files/37wic-monthly-6.pdf\\\",\\\"https://fns-prod.azureedge.us/sites/default/files/resource-files/37wic-monthly-5.pdf\\\"],\\\"runAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-27T13:29:28Z\\\",\\\"reasoning\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"heading\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"USDA FNS WIC total participants, March 2026 fixed vintage\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"The resolver is the USDA Food and Nutrition Service WIC Participation and Costs monthly table, national Total Participants, March 2026, first preliminary print. Because the official fixed-vintage PDF already included March 2026 at run time, this is treated as a post-release fixed-vintage cell with only transcription and vintage-selection uncertainty.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened the USDA FNS WIC Data Tables page to identify the official source family and available resource links.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"The official WIC Data Tables page listed FY 2026 preliminary monthly state-level data and Monthly Data - National Level, with page updated 2026-02-24 and links to official FNS resource files.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Opened the official FNS March-inclusive national monthly PDF at 37wic-monthly-6.pdf.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"The PDF states Data as of June 12, 2026; March 2026 values are Women 1,458,253, Infant 1,419,036, Children 3,824,372, Total Participants 6,701,661, Food Costs 431,316,601, NSA Costs 165,990,106, Average Food Cost 64.36.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Fetched same-vintage nearby official observations from the March-inclusive PDF.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Same-vintage FY 2026 recent totals were Nov 2025 6,771,734, Dec 2025 6,712,611, Jan 2026 6,696,300, Feb 2026 6,664,580, and Mar 2026 6,701,661.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Fetched the immediately prior official vintage to check the vintage boundary and revision behavior.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"The prior 37wic-monthly-5.pdf states Data as of May 8, 2026 and included Feb 2026 Total Participants 6,640,819 but did not include Mar 2026; therefore the June 12, 2026 PDF is the first fetched official print containing Mar 2026.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"tool\\\",\\\"tool\\\":\\\"official.lookup\\\",\\\"call\\\":\\\"Fetched the recent official-source reference class from the March-inclusive PDF and older official monthly rows.\\\",\\\"result\\\":\\\"Recent same-month and nearby totals were Mar 2025 6,850,836, Feb 2025 6,802,175, Apr 2025 6,877,215, Mar 2024 6,680,974, and Mar 2023 6,621,311.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Base-rate/reference-class view: March participation often sits above February, with Mar 2025 exceeding Feb 2025 by 48,661 and Mar 2024 exceeding Feb 2024 by 35,336. The same-vintage FY 2026 pattern is consistent with that seasonal rebound, from 6,664,580 in February to 6,701,661 in March.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Counter-consideration: if this needed an ex-ante forecast before the June 12 official vintage, the late-2025 downshift and February weakness would have argued for a wider interval around roughly the high-6.6-million to low-6.7-million range. Once the first official print is fetched, that uncertainty is dominated by avoiding later revisions and matching the printed whole-count precision.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"math\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Point uses the official first-print total directly: 1,458,253 women + 1,419,036 infants + 3,824,372 children = 6,701,661 total participants. The 80% interval is set to 6,701,660 to 6,701,662, one participant around the printed whole-count total, to reflect only transcription/vintage-selection risk after the official fixed vintage is observed.\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"forecast\\\",\\\"point\\\":6701661,\\\"ciLow\\\":6701660,\\\"ciHigh\\\":6701662}]}\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-34-28z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-april-to-june-2026-first-print-apr-jun-2026/normalized_cells.json:20:    \\\"label\\\": \\\"Nov 2025-Jan 2026 unemployment rate, percent\\\",\\nrecords/thesis-analyst/2026-06-27/2026-06-27t13-34-28z-ons-labour-unemployment-rate-april-to-june-2026-first-print-apr-jun-2026/revision_prompt.md:112:{\\\"slug\\\":\\\"uk-ons-unemployment-rate-apr-jun-2026-first-print\\\",\\\"country\\\":\\\"UK\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"data\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"UK unemployment Apr-Jun 2026\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"ONS UK unemployment rate for people aged 16 years and over, seasonally adjusted Labour Force Survey estimate, April to June 2026, first print\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"percent\\\",\\\"pointEstimate\\\":5.1,\\\"ciLow\\\":4.7,\\\"ciHigh\\\":5.5,\\\"confidence\\\":0.8,\\\"resolutionDate\\\":\\\"2026-08-11\\\",